{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540496311,"sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2f2e381002HNt6BU6wsANCkX","sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","messageID":"msg_1d2f2d6d7001TJRZu4zQYiKV35","type":"tool","id":"call_5458cc5615b840768092c824","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md, lines 1-239\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 11: typed-command-delivery-and-guards\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that generate one table of tracked commands, attach a typed command to the top recommendation, put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row, measure the typed block in the command capture and add the mirror visibility guard, hook health, a head length test and a brief cost script.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"typed command delivery tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 11: typed-command-delivery-and-guards\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a live model session, an arena or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `BLD` is `npm run build` in `ADV`, which must exit 0.\n31: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` its test `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `VCA` is `npx vitest run tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n32: - `DB` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. `DBC` is `node $DB --check | jq -r .status`, which must print `fresh`. `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md`.\n33: - `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `FT` is `$ADV/tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` (new) and `VFT` is `npx vitest run tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `AR` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`. `ART` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-typed-command.vitest.ts` (new) and `VART` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-typed-command.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n35: - `HT` is `$ADV/tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` (new) and `VHT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n36: - `CAP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `BASE` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json`. `CORPUS` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`. `RS` is `npx vitest run tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n37: - `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` (new). `OF` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`. `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`.\n38: - `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`. `ST` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`. `STT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` and `VST` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n39: - `SRM` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `SRMT` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/sync-runtime-mirrors.test.mjs` and `SRR` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`.\n40: - `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts`. `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DCT` is `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs $DS/tests/doctor-setup-orphan-line.test.cjs`. `IG` is `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n41: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print at least `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n42: - `EVAL` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which must print numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5.\n43: - `PY` is `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py`, which must exit 0. `PAR` is `npx vitest run tests/parity/python-ts-parity.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n44: \n45: Rules for every task:\n46: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it.\n47: - No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. A script filters on `split` before it uses a prompt and prints row ids only.\n48: - No worker starts a live model session. Running the Claude prompt hook or the advisor CLI is not a model session, and both run in a sandboxed socket directory here.\n49: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T024 checks it.\n50: - No task writes to the home folder, installs anything, edits `AGENTS.md`, renames a command or edits a file under `.skilled/commands/create/`.\n51: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n52: \n53: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n54: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`), T002 (`$SP/typed-before.json`). Read-only for the repository.\n55: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phases 005, 008 and 010 are committed, because they edit `AR`, `CA`, `ST`, `SCH`, `DSY`, `IG` and `RA`.\n56: - Wave 1: T003 (`DB`, `CA`), T004 (`SRM`, `SRMT`), T005 (`SCH`), T006 (`MBC`), T007 (`IG`).\n57: - Wave 2: T008 (`CA`, `CAT`), T009 (`ST`, `STT`), T010 (`DSY`), T011 (`SRR`).\n58: - Wave 3: T012 (`FU`, `FT`), T013 (`AR`, `ART`), T014 (`HT`).\n59: - Wave 4: T015 (`CAP`), T016 (`AR`).\n60: - Wave 5: T017 (`BASE`), T018 (`RA`), T019 (`CBR`).\n61: - Wave 6, one at a time because both start a sandboxed daemon: T020 (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`), T021 (`$SP/brief-cost.json`).\n62: - Verification, one at a time: T022, T023, T024, T025.\n63: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n68: ## Phase 1: Setup\n69: \n70: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3, .metrics.typed_reach_top3, .metrics.agreement, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.plain'`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `DBC`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VST`, `node --test $SRMT`, `node $SRM --check` and `DCT`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `node $SRM --check` exits 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 15. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\n71: - [x] T002 Record each typed row's state (`$SP/typed-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '[.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | endswith(\"-typed-01\")) | {id: .key, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1}] as $t | .attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [$t[] | . + {attached: ($a[.id] // null)}]' > $SP/typed-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 44, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 24 and `jq -r '.[] | keys[]' $SP/typed-before.json | sort -u | tr '\\n' ' '` prints `attached id top top1 `.\n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n77: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n78: \n79: ### Wave 1\n80: - [ ] T003 [P] Generate one table of every tracked command (`DB`, `CA`). In `CA`, above `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, add `export interface TrackedCommand { readonly policy: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string; readonly scorerRow: boolean; }` with a comment saying the table covers every tracked command, whether or not its bridge is active, so a typed command always has a policy and an owner. In `DB`'s `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)`, build a third map over every entry, with no enabled filter: key `entryRunnable(entry)`, value `{ policy: runnablePolicy(runnable, policies), ownerSkillId: entry.skillId, scorerRow: entry.runtime.typescript.enabled === true }`. Throw `[command-bridges] Conflicting tracked command <runnable>` when one runnable repeats with a different owner or policy. Render it after the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block as `export const TRACKED_COMMANDS: Readonly<Record<string, TrackedCommand>> = {` with one line per key in sorted order, shaped `  '<runnable>': { policy: '<policy>', ownerSkillId: '<owner>', scorerRow: <true|false> },`, and `};`. Run `node $DB`. Do not edit the generated block by hand. Verify: `DBC` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"scorerRow: (true|false) \\},$\" $CA` prints at least 44, `rg -n \"'/create:goal': \\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false \\},\" $CA` and `rg -n \"'/speckit:resume': \\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true \\},\" $CA` each print one line, `TC` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints nothing.\n81: - [ ] T004 [P] Add a command visibility count and a collapse guard to the mirror check (`SRM`, `SRMT`). Add `const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md'])` with a comment saying Claude Code reads a command folder holding `skill.md` as one skill and hides its siblings, and the existing case is kept until the commands are renamed. Add and export `commandVisibility(expectedLinks)`: it takes the `claude-commands` links whose path below `.claude/commands/` holds a folder, counts them as `total`, and counts Claude's `visible` as one per folder that holds `skill.md` plus every command in the other folders. Cursor's `visible` is `total`, because Cursor uses flat names. Add and export `collapseDrift(expectedLinks)`, which returns `COLLAPSE <folder>/skill.md hides <n> sibling commands on Claude Code` for each folder holding `skill.md` whose path is not in the allowlist. In `checkMirrors`, add those lines to `drift`, and before the PASS line print `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude <visible>/<total>, cursor <total>/<total>`. Keep the PASS line as it is. In `SRMT`, add one case where synthetic links for `create/skill.md`, `create/readme.md` and `deep/review.md` give `{ claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 }, cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 } }` and no drift, and one where an added `design/skill.md` beside `design/chart.md` gives `['COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Verify: `node --test $SRMT` reports `fail 0`, `node $SRM --check` prints a line containing `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` and exits 0, and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n82: - [ ] T005 [P] Add `hookHealth` to the status output schema (`SCH`). In `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema`, after `embeddingsHealth`, add `hookHealth: z.object({ invocations: z.number().int().positive(), rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(), rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1), rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1) }).strict().optional()`. Verify: `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \"hookHealth\" $SCH` prints 1 and `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n83: - [ ] T006 [P] Create `MBC`. `node $MBC [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` reads `CORPUS` under `--root` (default the current directory), keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, and with `--rows` keeps only the named ids, exiting 2 with `{\"error\":\"holdout_row\",\"id\":\"<id>\"}` for a row whose split is `holdout` and `{\"error\":\"unknown_row\",\"id\":\"<id>\"}` for an id it cannot find, before it spawns anything. It makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cost-'))`, and for each row pipes `{\"prompt\":<prompt>,\"cwd\":<root>,\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"cost-<id>\"}` into `node <root>/$HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory and a 30,000 ms timeout. It takes `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` (or the empty string), and records `bytes` as its UTF-8 length and `estimatedTokens` as `Math.ceil(bytes / 4)`, the renderer's own four characters per token. It prints one JSON object `{ rows: [{ id, bytes, estimatedTokens }], totalBytes, medianBytes, maxBytes }` and never prints a prompt. At the end it sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory and removes the directory. Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `node $MBC --rows cmd-speckit-save-typed-01 | jq -c '.rows[0] | [.id, (.bytes > 0), (.estimatedTokens == ((.bytes + 3) / 4 | floor))]'` prints `[\"cmd-speckit-save-typed-01\",true,true]`, `node $MBC --rows \"$(jq -r 'select(.split==\"holdout\") | .id' $CORPUS | head -1)\"` exits 2 and prints `holdout_row`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n84: - [ ] T007 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the paragraph about Codex hook approval: to see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Re-read the section first, because phase 008 also edits section 2. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor_recommend --json\" $IG` prints 1, and the documented command prints one line that is neither empty nor `null`.\n85: \n86: ### Wave 2\n87: - [ ] T008 [P] Add two typed command helpers (`CA`, `CAT`). `typedCommandIn(prompt)` lowercases the prompt and returns the longest `TRACKED_COMMANDS` key found at a position where the character before it is absent, whitespace, a backtick, a quote or `(`, and the character after it is absent or not a word character, colon or hyphen. It returns undefined when none is found. `typedCommandForTop(topSkillId, prompt)` takes that key and returns `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }` from its row when `topSkillId` is the row's `ownerSkillId` or `commandRowFor(topSkillId)?.command` equals the key, and undefined otherwise. In `CAT`, add cases: `/create:skill-parent deploy-hub with three modes` gives `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:sk` gives undefined, `see docs/create:goal.md` gives undefined, `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives `{ command: '/speckit:resume', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit' }`, `typedCommandForTop('command-speckit-resume', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives the same and `typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives undefined. Verify: `VCA` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T009 [P] Report hook health in the status (`ST`, `STT`). Run after phase 008, which edits `readSemanticLaneHealth` and `handleAdvisorStatus` in the same file. In `readAdvisorStatus`, in the `output` object of the success path (the one inside `try`, right after `laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,`), add `hookHealth` from `readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot)` (`$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`) when its `lastInvocations` is not empty: `invocations` is the length of `lastInvocations` and the three rolling fields copy over. Leave the error path as it is. Add a comment saying the p95 counts cache-hit invocations only. In `STT`, add one case that writes two valid diagnostic records with `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` for a temporary workspace root and reads `hookHealth.invocations` 2, and one case for a root with no records that reads no `hookHealth` key. Verify: `VST` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n89: - [ ] T010 [P] Show hook health under the setup advisor leg (`DSY`). Run after phase 008, which adds an embedder leg after this one. In the single list item that starts `- \"Leg advisor:`, append before its closing quote: ` When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.` Change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c \"hookHealth\" $DSY` prints 1 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n90: - [ ] T011 [P] In `SRR` section 5, add two sentences after the check command: the check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows, and it fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands. Verify: `rg -n \"skill.md\" $SRR` prints at least one line in section 5.\n91: \n92: ### Wave 3\n93: - [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n94: - [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n95: - [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\n96: \n97: ### Wave 4\n98: - [ ] T015 Add the typed block to the command capture (`CAP`). Import `typedCommandForTop` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from the built attach module the script already loads. For each row with `row_type` `typed`, compute `delivered` as `typedCommandForTop(topId, row.prompt)?.command ?? attached`, the same precedence as the handler, and `policy` as `TRACKED_COMMANDS[delivered]?.policy ?? null`. Count `own` when `top1Hit`, else `attached` when `delivered` equals the expected command and `policy` is not null, in a tally built with `emptyAttachedTally` and `addAttachedRow`. Add `typed: attachedTallyJson(...)` to `attachedMetrics`, and `typedRows`, keyed by row id in sorted order, each `{ expected_command, top, carried, command, policy }`, where `carried` is `own`, `attached` or null. Write no prompt text. Leave every existing key and its computation unchanged. Verify: after `BLD`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed'` prints `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.typedRows[] | keys] | unique'` prints `[[\"carried\",\"command\",\"expected_command\",\"policy\",\"top\"]]` and `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n99: - [ ] T016 Take a hub-attached command's policy from the new table (`AR`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, replace the spread that reads `COMMAND_POLICIES` with `...(Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command) ? { policy: TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy } : {})`, import `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and drop `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the import when nothing else uses it. Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $AR` prints nothing or 0, `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\[command\\]\" $AR` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `VART` reports 0 failed.\n100: \n101: ### Wave 5\n102: - [ ] T017 Rebuild and recapture the command baseline (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' $BASE` prints `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `jq '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3' $BASE` prints at least the value in `$SP/before.txt`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain' $BASE` equals the line in `$SP/before.txt` and `RS` reports 0 failed.\n103: - [ ] T018 [P] In `RA`, describe `attachedMetrics.typed` and `attachedMetrics.typedRows`, the rule that a typed command travels on its owner, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` with its flags, its output keys and its sandbox. Verify: `rg -c \"attachedMetrics.typed|typedRows|measure-brief-cost\" $RA` prints at least 3.\n104: - [ ] T019 [P] In `CBR`, describe `TRACKED_COMMANDS`: one row per bridge entry with its policy, its owner and `scorerRow`, generated whether or not the bridge is active. Verify: `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS|scorerRow\" $CBR` prints at least 2.\n105: \n106: ### Wave 6\n107: - [ ] T020 Check the real heads (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`). Write a script that reads `CORPUS`, keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))`, pipes each row's payload (the shape of T006, session id `typed-<id>`) into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to it, takes the first line of `additionalContext` and reads it with `parseOffer` from `OF`. It writes `[{ id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees }]` to `typed-heads.json`, where `commandMatches` compares the `/<namespace>:<name>` part of the offer with the row's `expected_command`, `policyPresent` is true for `run`, `start` or `ask` and `labelAgrees` compares the policy with the row's `expected_policy`. It stops and removes its sandbox as T006 does and prints no prompt. Verify: `jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints 44, `jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\",\")' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints `cmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n108: - [ ] T021 Measure the brief cost (`$SP/brief-cost.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost.json`. Verify: `jq '.rows | length' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints 44, `jq '.maxBytes > 0 and .medianBytes > 0' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints `true` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n109: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n114: ## Phase 3: Verification\n115: \n116: - [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\n117: - [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\"$D\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n118: - [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n119: - [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n120: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n125: ## Completion Criteria\n126: \n127: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n128: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n129: - [ ] The committed baseline reads `attachedMetrics.typed.combined` 44 of 44 and every floor holds against `scratch/before.txt`\n130: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n131: \n132: ---\n133: \n134: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n135: ## Cross-References\n136: \n137: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n138: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n139: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n140: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: ## Verification Checklist\n146: \n147: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n148: ## Verification Protocol\n149: \n150: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n151: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n152: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n153: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n154: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n155: \n156: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n157: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n162: ## Pre-Implementation\n163: \n164: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers and the typed row state are in `scratch/` (T001, T002).\n165: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The coordinator confirmed phases 005, 008 and 010 are committed before wave 1 started.\n166: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n167: \n168: ---\n169: \n170: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n171: ## Code Quality\n172: \n173: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0.\n174: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id (T024).\n175: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] The generated block is written by the deriver only, and its check prints `fresh` (T003, T022).\n176: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] A prompt with no typed command leaves the recommendation unchanged (T012, T013).\n177: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n178: \n179: ---\n180: \n181: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n182: ## Testing Checklist\n183: \n184: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T022).\n185: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The baseline reads 44 of 44 typed and the slice test passes (T017).\n186: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The parity test and the Python test pass (T022).\n187: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The real heads of all 44 typed rows carry their command and a policy (T020).\n188: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n189: \n190: ---\n191: \n192: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n193: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n194: \n195: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `delivery`: the scorer finds the owner, and the command is lost between the scorer and the head.\n196: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the policy table is listed: `rg -n \"COMMAND_POLICIES|TRACKED_COMMANDS\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'`.\n197: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P1] Both return paths of the recommend handler apply the typed step (T013).\n198: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n199: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n200: \n201: ---\n202: \n203: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n204: ## Security\n205: \n206: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task reads or prints holdout prompt text, and the cost script refuses a holdout row (T006).\n207: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No task writes to the home folder or installs anything (T024).\n208: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n209: \n210: ---\n211: \n212: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n213: ## Documentation\n214: \n215: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers.\n216: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The install guide, the setup asset and the three READMEs match the code (T007, T010, T011, T018, T019).\n217: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n218: \n219: ---\n220: \n221: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n222: ## File Organization\n223: \n224: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, measurements and the hook check live in `scratch/` only.\n225: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n226: \n227: ---\n228: \n229: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n230: ## Verification Summary\n231: \n232: | Category | Total | Verified |\n233: |----------|-------|----------|\n234: | P0 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n235: | P1 Items | 7 | 0/7 |\n236: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n237: \n238: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n239: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md, lines 1-239\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 11: typed-command-delivery-and-guards\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that generate one table of tracked commands, attach a typed command to the top recommendation, put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row, measure the typed block in the command capture and add the mirror visibility guard, hook health, a head length test and a brief cost script.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"typed command delivery tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 11: typed-command-delivery-and-guards\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a live model session, an arena or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `BLD` is `npm run build` in `ADV`, which must exit 0.\n31: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` its test `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `VCA` is `npx vitest run tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n32: - `DB` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. `DBC` is `node $DB --check | jq -r .status`, which must print `fresh`. `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md`.\n33: - `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `FT` is `$ADV/tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` (new) and `VFT` is `npx vitest run tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `AR` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`. `ART` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-typed-command.vitest.ts` (new) and `VART` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-typed-command.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n35: - `HT` is `$ADV/tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` (new) and `VHT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n36: - `CAP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `BASE` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json`. `CORPUS` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`. `RS` is `npx vitest run tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n37: - `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` (new). `OF` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`. `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`.\n38: - `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`. `ST` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`. `STT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` and `VST` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n39: - `SRM` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `SRMT` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/sync-runtime-mirrors.test.mjs` and `SRR` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`.\n40: - `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts`. `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DCT` is `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs $DS/tests/doctor-setup-orphan-line.test.cjs`. `IG` is `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n41: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print at least `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n42: - `EVAL` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which must print numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5.\n43: - `PY` is `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py`, which must exit 0. `PAR` is `npx vitest run tests/parity/python-ts-parity.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n44: \n45: Rules for every task:\n46: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it.\n47: - No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. A script filters on `split` before it uses a prompt and prints row ids only.\n48: - No worker starts a live model session. Running the Claude prompt hook or the advisor CLI is not a model session, and both run in a sandboxed socket directory here.\n49: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T024 checks it.\n50: - No task writes to the home folder, installs anything, edits `AGENTS.md`, renames a command or edits a file under `.skilled/commands/create/`.\n51: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n52: \n53: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n54: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`), T002 (`$SP/typed-before.json`). Read-only for the repository.\n55: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phases 005, 008 and 010 are committed, because they edit `AR`, `CA`, `ST`, `SCH`, `DSY`, `IG` and `RA`.\n56: - Wave 1: T003 (`DB`, `CA`), T004 (`SRM`, `SRMT`), T005 (`SCH`), T006 (`MBC`), T007 (`IG`).\n57: - Wave 2: T008 (`CA`, `CAT`), T009 (`ST`, `STT`), T010 (`DSY`), T011 (`SRR`).\n58: - Wave 3: T012 (`FU`, `FT`), T013 (`AR`, `ART`), T014 (`HT`).\n59: - Wave 4: T015 (`CAP`), T016 (`AR`).\n60: - Wave 5: T017 (`BASE`), T018 (`RA`), T019 (`CBR`).\n61: - Wave 6, one at a time because both start a sandboxed daemon: T020 (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`), T021 (`$SP/brief-cost.json`).\n62: - Verification, one at a time: T022, T023, T024, T025.\n63: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n68: ## Phase 1: Setup\n69: \n70: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3, .metrics.typed_reach_top3, .metrics.agreement, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.plain'`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `DBC`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VST`, `node --test $SRMT`, `node $SRM --check` and `DCT`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `node $SRM --check` exits 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 15. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\n71: - [x] T002 Record each typed row's state (`$SP/typed-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '[.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | endswith(\"-typed-01\")) | {id: .key, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1}] as $t | .attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [$t[] | . + {attached: ($a[.id] // null)}]' > $SP/typed-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 44, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 24 and `jq -r '.[] | keys[]' $SP/typed-before.json | sort -u | tr '\\n' ' '` prints `attached id top top1 `.\n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n77: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n78: \n79: ### Wave 1\n80: - [ ] T003 [P] Generate one table of every tracked command (`DB`, `CA`). In `CA`, above `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, add `export interface TrackedCommand { readonly policy: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string; readonly scorerRow: boolean; }` with a comment saying the table covers every tracked command, whether or not its bridge is active, so a typed command always has a policy and an owner. In `DB`'s `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)`, build a third map over every entry, with no enabled filter: key `entryRunnable(entry)`, value `{ policy: runnablePolicy(runnable, policies), ownerSkillId: entry.skillId, scorerRow: entry.runtime.typescript.enabled === true }`. Throw `[command-bridges] Conflicting tracked command <runnable>` when one runnable repeats with a different owner or policy. Render it after the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block as `export const TRACKED_COMMANDS: Readonly<Record<string, TrackedCommand>> = {` with one line per key in sorted order, shaped `  '<runnable>': { policy: '<policy>', ownerSkillId: '<owner>', scorerRow: <true|false> },`, and `};`. Run `node $DB`. Do not edit the generated block by hand. Verify: `DBC` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"scorerRow: (true|false) \\},$\" $CA` prints at least 44, `rg -n \"'/create:goal': \\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false \\},\" $CA` and `rg -n \"'/speckit:resume': \\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true \\},\" $CA` each print one line, `TC` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints nothing.\n81: - [ ] T004 [P] Add a command visibility count and a collapse guard to the mirror check (`SRM`, `SRMT`). Add `const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md'])` with a comment saying Claude Code reads a command folder holding `skill.md` as one skill and hides its siblings, and the existing case is kept until the commands are renamed. Add and export `commandVisibility(expectedLinks)`: it takes the `claude-commands` links whose path below `.claude/commands/` holds a folder, counts them as `total`, and counts Claude's `visible` as one per folder that holds `skill.md` plus every command in the other folders. Cursor's `visible` is `total`, because Cursor uses flat names. Add and export `collapseDrift(expectedLinks)`, which returns `COLLAPSE <folder>/skill.md hides <n> sibling commands on Claude Code` for each folder holding `skill.md` whose path is not in the allowlist. In `checkMirrors`, add those lines to `drift`, and before the PASS line print `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude <visible>/<total>, cursor <total>/<total>`. Keep the PASS line as it is. In `SRMT`, add one case where synthetic links for `create/skill.md`, `create/readme.md` and `deep/review.md` give `{ claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 }, cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 } }` and no drift, and one where an added `design/skill.md` beside `design/chart.md` gives `['COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Verify: `node --test $SRMT` reports `fail 0`, `node $SRM --check` prints a line containing `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` and exits 0, and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n82: - [ ] T005 [P] Add `hookHealth` to the status output schema (`SCH`). In `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema`, after `embeddingsHealth`, add `hookHealth: z.object({ invocations: z.number().int().positive(), rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(), rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1), rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1) }).strict().optional()`. Verify: `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \"hookHealth\" $SCH` prints 1 and `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n83: - [ ] T006 [P] Create `MBC`. `node $MBC [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` reads `CORPUS` under `--root` (default the current directory), keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, and with `--rows` keeps only the named ids, exiting 2 with `{\"error\":\"holdout_row\",\"id\":\"<id>\"}` for a row whose split is `holdout` and `{\"error\":\"unknown_row\",\"id\":\"<id>\"}` for an id it cannot find, before it spawns anything. It makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cost-'))`, and for each row pipes `{\"prompt\":<prompt>,\"cwd\":<root>,\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"cost-<id>\"}` into `node <root>/$HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory and a 30,000 ms timeout. It takes `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` (or the empty string), and records `bytes` as its UTF-8 length and `estimatedTokens` as `Math.ceil(bytes / 4)`, the renderer's own four characters per token. It prints one JSON object `{ rows: [{ id, bytes, estimatedTokens }], totalBytes, medianBytes, maxBytes }` and never prints a prompt. At the end it sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory and removes the directory. Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `node $MBC --rows cmd-speckit-save-typed-01 | jq -c '.rows[0] | [.id, (.bytes > 0), (.estimatedTokens == ((.bytes + 3) / 4 | floor))]'` prints `[\"cmd-speckit-save-typed-01\",true,true]`, `node $MBC --rows \"$(jq -r 'select(.split==\"holdout\") | .id' $CORPUS | head -1)\"` exits 2 and prints `holdout_row`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n84: - [ ] T007 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the paragraph about Codex hook approval: to see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Re-read the section first, because phase 008 also edits section 2. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor_recommend --json\" $IG` prints 1, and the documented command prints one line that is neither empty nor `null`.\n85: \n86: ### Wave 2\n87: - [ ] T008 [P] Add two typed command helpers (`CA`, `CAT`). `typedCommandIn(prompt)` lowercases the prompt and returns the longest `TRACKED_COMMANDS` key found at a position where the character before it is absent, whitespace, a backtick, a quote or `(`, and the character after it is absent or not a word character, colon or hyphen. It returns undefined when none is found. `typedCommandForTop(topSkillId, prompt)` takes that key and returns `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }` from its row when `topSkillId` is the row's `ownerSkillId` or `commandRowFor(topSkillId)?.command` equals the key, and undefined otherwise. In `CAT`, add cases: `/create:skill-parent deploy-hub with three modes` gives `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:sk` gives undefined, `see docs/create:goal.md` gives undefined, `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives `{ command: '/speckit:resume', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit' }`, `typedCommandForTop('command-speckit-resume', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives the same and `typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives undefined. Verify: `VCA` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T009 [P] Report hook health in the status (`ST`, `STT`). Run after phase 008, which edits `readSemanticLaneHealth` and `handleAdvisorStatus` in the same file. In `readAdvisorStatus`, in the `output` object of the success path (the one inside `try`, right after `laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,`), add `hookHealth` from `readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot)` (`$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`) when its `lastInvocations` is not empty: `invocations` is the length of `lastInvocations` and the three rolling fields copy over. Leave the error path as it is. Add a comment saying the p95 counts cache-hit invocations only. In `STT`, add one case that writes two valid diagnostic records with `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` for a temporary workspace root and reads `hookHealth.invocations` 2, and one case for a root with no records that reads no `hookHealth` key. Verify: `VST` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n89: - [ ] T010 [P] Show hook health under the setup advisor leg (`DSY`). Run after phase 008, which adds an embedder leg after this one. In the single list item that starts `- \"Leg advisor:`, append before its closing quote: ` When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.` Change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c \"hookHealth\" $DSY` prints 1 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n90: - [ ] T011 [P] In `SRR` section 5, add two sentences after the check command: the check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows, and it fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands. Verify: `rg -n \"skill.md\" $SRR` prints at least one line in section 5.\n91: \n92: ### Wave 3\n93: - [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n94: - [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n95: - [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\n96: \n97: ### Wave 4\n98: - [ ] T015 Add the typed block to the command capture (`CAP`). Import `typedCommandForTop` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from the built attach module the script already loads. For each row with `row_type` `typed`, compute `delivered` as `typedCommandForTop(topId, row.prompt)?.command ?? attached`, the same precedence as the handler, and `policy` as `TRACKED_COMMANDS[delivered]?.policy ?? null`. Count `own` when `top1Hit`, else `attached` when `delivered` equals the expected command and `policy` is not null, in a tally built with `emptyAttachedTally` and `addAttachedRow`. Add `typed: attachedTallyJson(...)` to `attachedMetrics`, and `typedRows`, keyed by row id in sorted order, each `{ expected_command, top, carried, command, policy }`, where `carried` is `own`, `attached` or null. Write no prompt text. Leave every existing key and its computation unchanged. Verify: after `BLD`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed'` prints `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.typedRows[] | keys] | unique'` prints `[[\"carried\",\"command\",\"expected_command\",\"policy\",\"top\"]]` and `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n99: - [ ] T016 Take a hub-attached command's policy from the new table (`AR`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, replace the spread that reads `COMMAND_POLICIES` with `...(Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command) ? { policy: TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy } : {})`, import `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and drop `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the import when nothing else uses it. Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $AR` prints nothing or 0, `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\[command\\]\" $AR` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `VART` reports 0 failed.\n100: \n101: ### Wave 5\n102: - [ ] T017 Rebuild and recapture the command baseline (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' $BASE` prints `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `jq '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3' $BASE` prints at least the value in `$SP/before.txt`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain' $BASE` equals the line in `$SP/before.txt` and `RS` reports 0 failed.\n103: - [ ] T018 [P] In `RA`, describe `attachedMetrics.typed` and `attachedMetrics.typedRows`, the rule that a typed command travels on its owner, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` with its flags, its output keys and its sandbox. Verify: `rg -c \"attachedMetrics.typed|typedRows|measure-brief-cost\" $RA` prints at least 3.\n104: - [ ] T019 [P] In `CBR`, describe `TRACKED_COMMANDS`: one row per bridge entry with its policy, its owner and `scorerRow`, generated whether or not the bridge is active. Verify: `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS|scorerRow\" $CBR` prints at least 2.\n105: \n106: ### Wave 6\n107: - [ ] T020 Check the real heads (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`). Write a script that reads `CORPUS`, keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))`, pipes each row's payload (the shape of T006, session id `typed-<id>`) into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to it, takes the first line of `additionalContext` and reads it with `parseOffer` from `OF`. It writes `[{ id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees }]` to `typed-heads.json`, where `commandMatches` compares the `/<namespace>:<name>` part of the offer with the row's `expected_command`, `policyPresent` is true for `run`, `start` or `ask` and `labelAgrees` compares the policy with the row's `expected_policy`. It stops and removes its sandbox as T006 does and prints no prompt. Verify: `jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints 44, `jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\",\")' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints `cmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n108: - [ ] T021 Measure the brief cost (`$SP/brief-cost.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost.json`. Verify: `jq '.rows | length' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints 44, `jq '.maxBytes > 0 and .medianBytes > 0' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints `true` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n109: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n114: ## Phase 3: Verification\n115: \n116: - [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\n117: - [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\"$D\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n118: - [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n119: - [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n120: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n125: ## Completion Criteria\n126: \n127: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n128: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n129: - [ ] The committed baseline reads `attachedMetrics.typed.combined` 44 of 44 and every floor holds against `scratch/before.txt`\n130: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n131: \n132: ---\n133: \n134: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n135: ## Cross-References\n136: \n137: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n138: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n139: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n140: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: ## Verification Checklist\n146: \n147: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n148: ## Verification Protocol\n149: \n150: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n151: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n152: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n153: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n154: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n155: \n156: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n157: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n162: ## Pre-Implementation\n163: \n164: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers and the typed row state are in `scratch/` (T001, T002).\n165: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The coordinator confirmed phases 005, 008 and 010 are committed before wave 1 started.\n166: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n167: \n168: ---\n169: \n170: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n171: ## Code Quality\n172: \n173: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0.\n174: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id (T024).\n175: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] The generated block is written by the deriver only, and its check prints `fresh` (T003, T022).\n176: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] A prompt with no typed command leaves the recommendation unchanged (T012, T013).\n177: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n178: \n179: ---\n180: \n181: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n182: ## Testing Checklist\n183: \n184: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T022).\n185: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The baseline reads 44 of 44 typed and the slice test passes (T017).\n186: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The parity test and the Python test pass (T022).\n187: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The real heads of all 44 typed rows carry their command and a policy (T020).\n188: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n189: \n190: ---\n191: \n192: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n193: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n194: \n195: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `delivery`: the scorer finds the owner, and the command is lost between the scorer and the head.\n196: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the policy table is listed: `rg -n \"COMMAND_POLICIES|TRACKED_COMMANDS\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'`.\n197: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P1] Both return paths of the recommend handler apply the typed step (T013).\n198: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n199: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n200: \n201: ---\n202: \n203: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n204: ## Security\n205: \n206: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task reads or prints holdout prompt text, and the cost script refuses a holdout row (T006).\n207: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No task writes to the home folder or installs anything (T024).\n208: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n209: \n210: ---\n211: \n212: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n213: ## Documentation\n214: \n215: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers.\n216: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The install guide, the setup asset and the three READMEs match the code (T007, T010, T011, T018, T019).\n217: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n218: \n219: ---\n220: \n221: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n222: ## File Organization\n223: \n224: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, measurements and the hook check live in `scratch/` only.\n225: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n226: \n227: ---\n228: \n229: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n230: ## Verification Summary\n231: \n232: | Category | Total | Verified |\n233: |----------|-------|----------|\n234: | P0 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n235: | P1 Items | 7 | 0/7 |\n236: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n237: \n238: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n239: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540495745,"end":1794540496311}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794540497444,"sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","part":{"id":"prt_1d2f2ea240012rAfs3H7rhVXyn","sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","messageID":"msg_1d2f2d6d7001TJRZu4zQYiKV35","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"ab1fa5a0defe8842be29252f961618baea46e8de","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":17197,"output":105,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":384,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794540499218,"sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","part":{"id":"prt_1d2f2f11200155QnaTX2pyyN70","sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","messageID":"msg_1d2f2ea28001NP75FTcpFEm1Pe","type":"step-start","snapshot":"d5f811876aa26657494442afbd57bbf7b855cdea"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540502447,"sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2f2fcee001F91Dc3GhG4SDEi","sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","messageID":"msg_1d2f2ea28001NP75FTcpFEm1Pe","type":"tool","id":"call_a04c62bf9fbe43b08575739f","tool":"skill","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"id":"sk-code"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"sk-code\">\n# Skill: sk-code\n\n<!-- Keywords: sk-code, code, surface-aware, two-axis, opencode, typescript, python, shell, json, jsonc, github-actions, ci-workflow, sk-code-quality, sk-code-review, sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend, quality, code-review, verification, debug, implement, workflow-doctrine, mode-registry, workflowmode, packetkind, backendkind, surface-router, evidence-base, surface-packet, guard, adapter, stderr, detector -->\n\n# Code Family Hub (sk-code)\n\nOne skill has two axes, one shared surface-detection router and one advisor identity.\nThe **workflow axis** has two code modes that act: sk-code-quality and sk-code-review.\nThe **surface axis** has three read-only evidence packets the hub bundles alongside a workflow mode: sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend and sk-code-skilled.\nEach packet carries the shared **implement → debug → verify** workflow doctrine (`shared/references/workflow-*.md`, symlinked in) plus its own domain knowledge.\nThis hub holds NO per-mode logic. It routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each mode or surface keeps its own contract in its packet.\n\n**Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`.\n`description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value. Each hub-root JSON routing file therefore states the same release.\n`ROUTER.md` and `README.md` keep their own document versions, as the frontmatter-versioning standard gives every doc but `SKILL.md`.\nThe authority stops at the hub root. Each `modes[]` packet carries its own version and release cadence.\nA packet version is independent of this one by design, so a gap between them is not drift.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\nUse this skill for code-family workflows. Invoke it as `sk-code` with an optional mode hint such as `quality: <request>`. The hub classifies the request, resolves a mode key, and loads the matching nested packet.\n\n**Workflow axis** (modes that act, one of them chosen as primary):\n\n| Mode | Use it for | Packet |\n|------|------------|--------|\n| **sk-code-quality** | Quality gate, P0/P1/P2 author checks, comment hygiene and surface checklists. | `sk-code/sk-code-quality/` |\n| **sk-code-review** | Findings-first review, security and correctness baseline, checklists, output contract and PR-state gates. | `sk-code/sk-code-review/` |\n\n**Surface axis** (read-only, advisor-invisible evidence. When a workflow mode scores, the hub bundles the surface after that primary mode. When no workflow mode scores, the hub routes the surface alone for a lookup, implement, debug or verify task, and the acting agent hands the author gates to `sk-code-quality` before it claims completion):\n\n| Surface | Carries | Packet |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| **sk-code-ci** | GitHub Actions evidence: trigger, filter, permission, timeout, concurrency and caching rules, the protected set, the intentional message-contract exception and the scaffold templates, with the repository-specific values read from a CI profile. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-ci/` |\n| **sk-code-frontend** | Stack-agnostic frontend evidence: web markup and CSS, web layout and accessibility, visual values, visual hierarchy and review, motion and interaction, the `tokens.css` starter tokens and Figma-to-code checks. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` |\n| **sk-code-skilled** | System-code evidence: TypeScript/Python/shell/config standards, hooks, alignment verification, authoring checklists. Bundles the implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine (read-only evidence) for the Skilled surface, and the acting agent applies it. | `sk-code/sk-code-skilled/` |\n\n**Surface list.** The hub has exactly three surfaces:\n- SKILLED (`sk-code-skilled`): the native surface for this framework's own code.\n- CI (`sk-code-ci`): the GitHub Actions workflow standards surface.\n- Frontend (`sk-code-frontend`): the stack-agnostic web practice and Figma-to-code surface, with visual values, visual hierarchy and review, and motion and interaction guidance, bundled from request vocabulary alone.\n\nThe hub also has two workflow modes: quality (`sk-code-quality`) and review (`sk-code-review`).\nAny other sk-code doc that counts surfaces points to this sentence.\n\n### When NOT to Use\n- Documentation-only changes with no code-work contract - use `sk-doc`.\n- Git workflow, branch, commit, PR, merge, or release work - use `sk-git`.\n- Pure browser inspection or external MCP transport work - use the relevant MCP skill.\n- For a measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source), use `sk-design-md-generator` first.\n- When a request or a frame leaves a visual value open (spacing, type, color, radius, shadow or motion), or a value sits off every token and scale, load `sk-code-frontend` and decide it from its visual-values reference.\n- Backend support primitives in `shared/` - they are consumed by the modes, not invoked as a user workflow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nRouting is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\nStage 1 (hub → mode) uses `hub-router.json` as the authored mode vocabulary. `mode-registry.json` carries the packet contracts, whose aliases are checked against that vocabulary.\nStage 2 (mode → leaves) uses the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) as the authored leaf-set router.\nBoth files point back here instead of restating the split.\n\nThe advisor routes every code query to the single identity `sk-code`. Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-code --prompt \"<task>\"` and follow the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\nCompiled routing is the default. The legacy fallback, the kill-switch and the `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST` live in the compiled-routing section of [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md).\n\nA bare implement, debug or verify request with no workflow mode becomes a pure surface bundle, and an unclear code intent asks for disambiguation. Neither path forces a stale default.\nRun the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Terms\n\n- **`workflowMode`**: the public mode or surface key a request resolves to.\n- **`packetKind`**: the axis a packet sits on, `workflow` for a mode that acts and `surface` for read-only evidence bundled alongside a mode.\n- **`backendKind`**: which backend runs the packet, `surface-router` or `review-cache` for a workflow mode and `evidence-base` for a surface.\n- **`surfaceBundle`**: the `routerPolicy.outcomes` entry where one workflow mode leads and zero or more surfaces follow as evidence.\n- **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each mode's discriminator, `surfaceDetection` markers and `advisorRouting`.\n- **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's `routerSignals`, `vocabularyClasses` and the surface-bundling policy.\n- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, plus the `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES` list and the always-loaded `DEFAULT_RESOURCE` preamble.\n- **shared control**: a hub-level resource declared in `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`, which resolves on disk and never projects as a leaf.\n- **leaf**: a typed `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n- **surface detection**: the shared detection order over the declared surfaces, which tries each specific surface first, then the `SKILLED` fallback, then `UNKNOWN`.\n- **`--surface-hint`**: the front-door flag that carries the detected surface into the compiled route, so a hinted surface leads a keyword tie.\n- **`UNKNOWN_FALLBACK`**: the load level the router returns, with a disambiguation checklist, when no mode resolves.\n\n### Layout\n```\nsk-code/\n  SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-mode code logic)\n  README.md              # human-facing front page for the hub\n  ROUTER.md              # active stage-two surface router and shared-control declaration\n  mode-registry.json     # the two-axis discriminator + advisorRouting contract\n  hub-router.json        # lexical routing signals + surfaceBundle policy for hub-local choice\n  description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n  graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n  leaf-manifest.json     # typed (workflowMode, leaf) pairs the router guards validate\n  changelog/             # hub release notes, one v<version>.md per hub release\n  feature-catalog/       # current-state inventory of the hub's routing capabilities\n  manual-testing-playbook/  # routing and disambiguation scenarios for the hub\n  benchmark/             # historical routing benchmark inputs and reports\n  sk-code-quality/       # quality mode packet     (workflow)\n  sk-code-review/        # review mode packet      (workflow)\n  sk-code-ci/            # GitHub Actions workflow standards packet (read-only evidence; rules, protected set and scaffold templates)\n  sk-code-frontend/      # stack-agnostic web and Figma-to-code evidence packet (read-only; references/web-visual-values.md, web-visual-hierarchy.md and web-motion-and-interaction.md plus assets/tokens.css)\n  sk-code-skilled/      # skilled surface packet (read-only evidence; carries the workflow doctrine)\n  shared/                # shared surface-detection router, cross-mode helpers, and the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine (references/workflow-*.md)\n```\n\nEach mode or surface packet is self-contained and carries no per-packet `graph-metadata.json`. Only this hub carries one, so the advisor discovers exactly one code skill identity. The implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine is a single shared source under `shared/references/`, and each surface symlinks it in rather than duplicating it.\n\n### Backend\nThe `surface-router` backend is the shared surface-detection router under `shared/`.\nIt centralizes the detection order over the declared surfaces, the SKILLED fallback and UNKNOWN.\nIt carries the shared implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine consumed by each surface.\nThe `review-cache` backend supports the sk-code-review mode's non-mutating review output cache.\nThe `evidence-base` backend serves the surface packets as read-only domain evidence (`sk-code-ci/`, `sk-code-frontend/`, `sk-code-skilled/`). The hub bundles them alongside the primary mode.\nThe packet mutates nothing and never carries process. The acting agent applies the doctrine it bundles.\nShared backend material provides surface identity, the workflow doctrine and cross-mode helpers.\nIt must never gain per-mode workflow contracts.\n\nThe **implement → debug → verify** phases are not standalone modes.\nTheir surface-agnostic doctrine lives once in `shared/references/workflow-implement.md`, `workflow-debug.md` and `workflow-verify.md`.\nThose files are symlinked into each surface, so the active surface carries the full workflow.\nA request to implement, debug or verify code causes the router to detect its surface and load that surface's bundled doctrine.\nThe acting agent applies that doctrine.\n\n### Maintenance\n\nAfter adding or removing a surface, run `/doctor:sk-code setup`. It checks the hub and names the repair for each failing check.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n- **ALWAYS** resolve a mode through `mode-registry.json`, and never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n- **ALWAYS** keep mode contracts in the mode packets, so the hub stays routing-only.\n- **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one skill identity.\n- **ALWAYS** give every mode an `advisorRouting` block with `routingClass: \"metadata\"` and the correct `packetSkillName`.\n- **ALWAYS** keep the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine as one shared source under `shared/references/`, symlinked into each surface, and never fork per-surface copies.\n- **ALWAYS** keep `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` keys aligned with its intent keys and packet leaves aligned with `leaf-manifest.json`.\n- **ALWAYS** keep hub-shared map inputs explicit in `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`, because they are control resources and never typed leaves.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n- **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a mode packet or `shared/`.\n- **NEVER** put per-mode quality, review, or surface workflow logic in the hub.\n- **NEVER** hardcode a router mapping outside `mode-registry.json`.\n- **NEVER** reintroduce implement, debug, or verify as standalone mode packets, because they are surface-owned doctrine.\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n- A new code mode is needed - extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet. Do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n- Surface identity and workflow ownership conflict in a way the shared router cannot classify.\n\n---\n\n## 5. REFERENCES\n\n- Workflow mode packets: `sk-code-quality/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-review/SKILL.md`.\n- Surface evidence packets: `sk-code-ci/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md`.\n- Shared workflow doctrine: `shared/references/workflow-implement.md`, `shared/references/workflow-debug.md`, `shared/references/workflow-verify.md` (symlinked into each surface).\n- Registry: `mode-registry.json` (two-axis: `packetKind` discriminates workflow vs surface).\n- Hub router signals + surface bundling: `hub-router.json`.\n- Surface router and shared controls: `ROUTER.md`.\n- Parent-skill pattern: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`.\n- Sibling example: `.skilled/skills/sk-prompt/`.\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/ROUTER.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/failed-runs.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/findings-and-recommendations.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/results.csv</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/skill-benchmark-report.json</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/skill-benchmark-report.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/source.md</file>\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","title":"skill","metadata":{"metadata":{"name":"sk-code","directory":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code","truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<skill_content name=\"sk-code\">\n# Skill: sk-code\n\n<!-- Keywords: sk-code, code, surface-aware, two-axis, opencode, typescript, python, shell, json, jsonc, github-actions, ci-workflow, sk-code-quality, sk-code-review, sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend, quality, code-review, verification, debug, implement, workflow-doctrine, mode-registry, workflowmode, packetkind, backendkind, surface-router, evidence-base, surface-packet, guard, adapter, stderr, detector -->\n\n# Code Family Hub (sk-code)\n\nOne skill has two axes, one shared surface-detection router and one advisor identity.\nThe **workflow axis** has two code modes that act: sk-code-quality and sk-code-review.\nThe **surface axis** has three read-only evidence packets the hub bundles alongside a workflow mode: sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend and sk-code-skilled.\nEach packet carries the shared **implement → debug → verify** workflow doctrine (`shared/references/workflow-*.md`, symlinked in) plus its own domain knowledge.\nThis hub holds NO per-mode logic. It routes by `workflowMode` through `mode-registry.json`, and each mode or surface keeps its own contract in its packet.\n\n**Version authority.** This file's `version` frontmatter is the hub's release version and matches the newest entry under `changelog/`.\n`description.json`, `mode-registry.json` and `hub-router.json` carry the same value. Each hub-root JSON routing file therefore states the same release.\n`ROUTER.md` and `README.md` keep their own document versions, as the frontmatter-versioning standard gives every doc but `SKILL.md`.\nThe authority stops at the hub root. Each `modes[]` packet carries its own version and release cadence.\nA packet version is independent of this one by design, so a gap between them is not drift.\n\n---\n\n## 1. WHEN TO USE\n\nUse this skill for code-family workflows. Invoke it as `sk-code` with an optional mode hint such as `quality: <request>`. The hub classifies the request, resolves a mode key, and loads the matching nested packet.\n\n**Workflow axis** (modes that act, one of them chosen as primary):\n\n| Mode | Use it for | Packet |\n|------|------------|--------|\n| **sk-code-quality** | Quality gate, P0/P1/P2 author checks, comment hygiene and surface checklists. | `sk-code/sk-code-quality/` |\n| **sk-code-review** | Findings-first review, security and correctness baseline, checklists, output contract and PR-state gates. | `sk-code/sk-code-review/` |\n\n**Surface axis** (read-only, advisor-invisible evidence. When a workflow mode scores, the hub bundles the surface after that primary mode. When no workflow mode scores, the hub routes the surface alone for a lookup, implement, debug or verify task, and the acting agent hands the author gates to `sk-code-quality` before it claims completion):\n\n| Surface | Carries | Packet |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| **sk-code-ci** | GitHub Actions evidence: trigger, filter, permission, timeout, concurrency and caching rules, the protected set, the intentional message-contract exception and the scaffold templates, with the repository-specific values read from a CI profile. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-ci/` |\n| **sk-code-frontend** | Stack-agnostic frontend evidence: web markup and CSS, web layout and accessibility, visual values, visual hierarchy and review, motion and interaction, the `tokens.css` starter tokens and Figma-to-code checks. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` |\n| **sk-code-skilled** | System-code evidence: TypeScript/Python/shell/config standards, hooks, alignment verification, authoring checklists. Bundles the implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine (read-only evidence) for the Skilled surface, and the acting agent applies it. | `sk-code/sk-code-skilled/` |\n\n**Surface list.** The hub has exactly three surfaces:\n- SKILLED (`sk-code-skilled`): the native surface for this framework's own code.\n- CI (`sk-code-ci`): the GitHub Actions workflow standards surface.\n- Frontend (`sk-code-frontend`): the stack-agnostic web practice and Figma-to-code surface, with visual values, visual hierarchy and review, and motion and interaction guidance, bundled from request vocabulary alone.\n\nThe hub also has two workflow modes: quality (`sk-code-quality`) and review (`sk-code-review`).\nAny other sk-code doc that counts surfaces points to this sentence.\n\n### When NOT to Use\n- Documentation-only changes with no code-work contract - use `sk-doc`.\n- Git workflow, branch, commit, PR, merge, or release work - use `sk-git`.\n- Pure browser inspection or external MCP transport work - use the relevant MCP skill.\n- For a measured Style Reference (design tokens extracted from a live source), use `sk-design-md-generator` first.\n- When a request or a frame leaves a visual value open (spacing, type, color, radius, shadow or motion), or a value sits off every token and scale, load `sk-code-frontend` and decide it from its visual-values reference.\n- Backend support primitives in `shared/` - they are consumed by the modes, not invoked as a user workflow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SMART ROUTING\n\nRouting is **registry-driven at runtime and authored in `hub-router.json`** in two stages.\nStage 1 (hub → mode) uses `hub-router.json` as the authored mode vocabulary. `mode-registry.json` carries the packet contracts, whose aliases are checked against that vocabulary.\nStage 2 (mode → leaves) uses the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) as the authored leaf-set router.\nBoth files point back here instead of restating the split.\n\nThe advisor routes every code query to the single identity `sk-code`. Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-code --prompt \"<task>\"` and follow the decision: `route` loads its `targets`, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\nCompiled routing is the default. The legacy fallback, the kill-switch and the `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST` live in the compiled-routing section of [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md).\n\nA bare implement, debug or verify request with no workflow mode becomes a pure surface bundle, and an unclear code intent asks for disambiguation. Neither path forces a stale default.\nRun the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HOW IT WORKS\n\n### Terms\n\n- **`workflowMode`**: the public mode or surface key a request resolves to.\n- **`packetKind`**: the axis a packet sits on, `workflow` for a mode that acts and `surface` for read-only evidence bundled alongside a mode.\n- **`backendKind`**: which backend runs the packet, `surface-router` or `review-cache` for a workflow mode and `evidence-base` for a surface.\n- **`surfaceBundle`**: the `routerPolicy.outcomes` entry where one workflow mode leads and zero or more surfaces follow as evidence.\n- **`mode-registry.json`**: the registry that owns each mode's discriminator, `surfaceDetection` markers and `advisorRouting`.\n- **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's `routerSignals`, `vocabularyClasses` and the surface-bundling policy.\n- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP`, plus the `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES` list and the always-loaded `DEFAULT_RESOURCE` preamble.\n- **shared control**: a hub-level resource declared in `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`, which resolves on disk and never projects as a leaf.\n- **leaf**: a typed `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair from `leaf-manifest.json` that a `RESOURCE_MAP` path converts to.\n- **surface detection**: the shared detection order over the declared surfaces, which tries each specific surface first, then the `SKILLED` fallback, then `UNKNOWN`.\n- **`--surface-hint`**: the front-door flag that carries the detected surface into the compiled route, so a hinted surface leads a keyword tie.\n- **`UNKNOWN_FALLBACK`**: the load level the router returns, with a disambiguation checklist, when no mode resolves.\n\n### Layout\n```\nsk-code/\n  SKILL.md               # this routing hub (no per-mode code logic)\n  README.md              # human-facing front page for the hub\n  ROUTER.md              # active stage-two surface router and shared-control declaration\n  mode-registry.json     # the two-axis discriminator + advisorRouting contract\n  hub-router.json        # lexical routing signals + surfaceBundle policy for hub-local choice\n  description.json       # hub advisor descriptor\n  graph-metadata.json    # the ONE advisor identity for the whole skill\n  leaf-manifest.json     # typed (workflowMode, leaf) pairs the router guards validate\n  changelog/             # hub release notes, one v<version>.md per hub release\n  feature-catalog/       # current-state inventory of the hub's routing capabilities\n  manual-testing-playbook/  # routing and disambiguation scenarios for the hub\n  benchmark/             # historical routing benchmark inputs and reports\n  sk-code-quality/       # quality mode packet     (workflow)\n  sk-code-review/        # review mode packet      (workflow)\n  sk-code-ci/            # GitHub Actions workflow standards packet (read-only evidence; rules, protected set and scaffold templates)\n  sk-code-frontend/      # stack-agnostic web and Figma-to-code evidence packet (read-only; references/web-visual-values.md, web-visual-hierarchy.md and web-motion-and-interaction.md plus assets/tokens.css)\n  sk-code-skilled/      # skilled surface packet (read-only evidence; carries the workflow doctrine)\n  shared/                # shared surface-detection router, cross-mode helpers, and the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine (references/workflow-*.md)\n```\n\nEach mode or surface packet is self-contained and carries no per-packet `graph-metadata.json`. Only this hub carries one, so the advisor discovers exactly one code skill identity. The implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine is a single shared source under `shared/references/`, and each surface symlinks it in rather than duplicating it.\n\n### Backend\nThe `surface-router` backend is the shared surface-detection router under `shared/`.\nIt centralizes the detection order over the declared surfaces, the SKILLED fallback and UNKNOWN.\nIt carries the shared implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine consumed by each surface.\nThe `review-cache` backend supports the sk-code-review mode's non-mutating review output cache.\nThe `evidence-base` backend serves the surface packets as read-only domain evidence (`sk-code-ci/`, `sk-code-frontend/`, `sk-code-skilled/`). The hub bundles them alongside the primary mode.\nThe packet mutates nothing and never carries process. The acting agent applies the doctrine it bundles.\nShared backend material provides surface identity, the workflow doctrine and cross-mode helpers.\nIt must never gain per-mode workflow contracts.\n\nThe **implement → debug → verify** phases are not standalone modes.\nTheir surface-agnostic doctrine lives once in `shared/references/workflow-implement.md`, `workflow-debug.md` and `workflow-verify.md`.\nThose files are symlinked into each surface, so the active surface carries the full workflow.\nA request to implement, debug or verify code causes the router to detect its surface and load that surface's bundled doctrine.\nThe acting agent applies that doctrine.\n\n### Maintenance\n\nAfter adding or removing a surface, run `/doctor:sk-code setup`. It checks the hub and names the repair for each failing check.\n\n---\n\n## 4. RULES\n\n### ✅ ALWAYS\n- **ALWAYS** resolve a mode through `mode-registry.json`, and never hardcode a router mapping in the hub.\n- **ALWAYS** keep mode contracts in the mode packets, so the hub stays routing-only.\n- **ALWAYS** keep exactly one `graph-metadata.json` (this hub's) so the advisor sees one skill identity.\n- **ALWAYS** give every mode an `advisorRouting` block with `routingClass: \"metadata\"` and the correct `packetSkillName`.\n- **ALWAYS** keep the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine as one shared source under `shared/references/`, symlinked into each surface, and never fork per-surface copies.\n- **ALWAYS** keep `ROUTER.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` keys aligned with its intent keys and packet leaves aligned with `leaf-manifest.json`.\n- **ALWAYS** keep hub-shared map inputs explicit in `SHARED_CONTROL_RESOURCES`, because they are control resources and never typed leaves.\n\n### ⛔ NEVER\n- **NEVER** add a `graph-metadata.json` inside a mode packet or `shared/`.\n- **NEVER** put per-mode quality, review, or surface workflow logic in the hub.\n- **NEVER** hardcode a router mapping outside `mode-registry.json`.\n- **NEVER** reintroduce implement, debug, or verify as standalone mode packets, because they are surface-owned doctrine.\n\n### ⚠️ ESCALATE IF\n- A new code mode is needed - extend `mode-registry.json` and open a packet. Do not bolt logic onto the hub.\n- Surface identity and workflow ownership conflict in a way the shared router cannot classify.\n\n---\n\n## 5. REFERENCES\n\n- Workflow mode packets: `sk-code-quality/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-review/SKILL.md`.\n- Surface evidence packets: `sk-code-ci/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md`.\n- Shared workflow doctrine: `shared/references/workflow-implement.md`, `shared/references/workflow-debug.md`, `shared/references/workflow-verify.md` (symlinked into each surface).\n- Registry: `mode-registry.json` (two-axis: `packetKind` discriminates workflow vs surface).\n- Hub router signals + surface bundling: `hub-router.json`.\n- Surface router and shared controls: `ROUTER.md`.\n- Parent-skill pattern: `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md`.\n- Sibling example: `.skilled/skills/sk-prompt/`.\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/ROUTER.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/README.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/failed-runs.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/findings-and-recommendations.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/results.csv</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/skill-benchmark-report.json</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/skill-benchmark-report.md</file>\n<file>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.opencode/skills/sk-code/benchmark/reports/2026-06-01--after--router/source.md</file>\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"id\":\"sk-code\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540502254,"end":1794540502447}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540502452,"sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2f2fb07001xOEaJ0f7usQm1O","sessionID":"ses_e2d0d5b5affeRgStbHfgZ2H3AM","messageID":"msg_1d2f2ea28001NP75FTcpFEm1Pe","type":"tool","id":"call_1ecb47ad4a4340ffad94aaba","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts, lines 1-732\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: advisor_recommend Handler\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\n10: import { readFileSync, realpathSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { resolve } from 'node:path';\n12: \n13: import { COMMAND_POLICIES, attachCommand, commandRowFor, typedCommandForTop } from '../lib/command-attach.js';\n14: import { advisorPromptCache } from '../lib/prompt-cache.js';\n15: import {\n16:   resolveAdvisorThresholdConfig,\n17: } from '../lib/skill-advisor-brief.js';\n18: import { scoreAdvisorPrompt } from '../lib/scorer/fusion.js';\n19: import {\n20:   DEEP_ROUTING_PROJECTION_HASH,\n21:   MERGED_DEEP_SKILL_ID,\n22:   modeForAlias,\n23:   modeForPromptAlias,\n24: } from '../lib/scorer/aliases.js';\n25: import {\n26:   getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth,\n27:   withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding,\n28: } from '../lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.js';\n29: import { DEFAULT_SHADOW_SCORER_LANE_WEIGHTS } from '../lib/scorer/lane-registry.js';\n30: import { sanitizeSkillLabel } from '../lib/render.js';\n31: import { recordShadowDelta, shadowDeltaSinkEnabled } from '../lib/shadow/shadow-sink.js';\n32: import { findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot } from '../lib/utils/workspace-root.js';\n33: import {\n34:   AdvisorRecommendInputSchema,\n35:   AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema,\n36:   type AdvisorRecommendInput,\n37:   type AdvisorRecommendOutput,\n38: } from '../schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.js';\n39: import { readAdvisorStatus } from './advisor-status.js';\n40: import {\n41:   COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS,\n42:   compiledRoutingEnabledForHub,\n43:   parseCompiledRoutingFlagMode,\n44: } from '../lib/compiled-routing-flag.js';\n45: import type { AdvisorScoringOptions } from '../lib/scorer/types.js';\n46: \n47: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n48: // 2. TYPE DEFINITIONS\n49: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n50: \n51: type HandlerResponse = { content: Array<{ type: string; text: string }> };\n52: type AdvisorStatus = ReturnType<typeof readAdvisorStatus>;\n53: type ScoredRecommendation = ReturnType<typeof scoreAdvisorPrompt>['recommendations'][number];\n54: type PublicRecommendationStatus = NonNullable<AdvisorRecommendOutput['recommendations'][number]['status']>;\n55: type PublicThresholds = AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'];\n56: type ShadowRecommendation = NonNullable<AdvisorRecommendOutput['_shadow']>['recommendations'][number];\n57: \n58: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n59: // 3. HELPERS\n60: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n61: \n62: // Emit-only, stderr, debug-gated compiled-routing diagnostic. Never written to\n63: // stdout or the tool response, and never changes the recommendation outcome.\n64: function emitCompiledRoutingBreadcrumb(message: string): void {\n65:   if (process.env.SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING_DEBUG) {\n66:     process.stderr.write(`[compiled-routing] ${message}\\n`);\n67:   }\n68: }\n69: \n70: function findWorkspaceRoot(start = process.cwd()): string {\n71:   return findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot(start, { maxDepth: 12 });\n72: }\n73: \n74: // Canonicalize a caller-supplied workspaceRoot via realpath.\n75: // The schema-level allowlist refinement runs against the same canonical\n76: // form, so a caller passing /tmp/symlink-to-repo gets the real path\n77: // post-symlink before downstream code uses it.\n78: function canonicalizeWorkspaceRoot(input: string): string {\n79:   const resolved = resolve(input);\n80:   try {\n81:     return realpathSync.native(resolved);\n82:   } catch {\n83:     return resolved;\n84:   }\n85: }\n86: \n87: function cacheSourceSignature(status: AdvisorStatus): string {\n88:   return `${status.freshness}:${status.generation}:${status.lastGenerationBump ?? 'never'}:${DEEP_ROUTING_PROJECTION_HASH}`;\n89: }\n90: \n91: function recommendationLabels(output: AdvisorRecommendOutput): string[] {\n92:   return output.recommendations.map((recommendation) => recommendation.skillId);\n93: }\n94: \n95: function unavailableTrustState(reason: string): AdvisorRecommendOutput['trustState'] {\n96:   return {\n97:     state: 'unavailable',\n98:     reason,\n99:     generation: 0,\n100:     checkedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n101:     lastLiveAt: null,\n102:   };\n103: }\n104: \n105: function publicThresholds(args: {\n106:   confidenceThreshold?: number;\n107:   uncertaintyThreshold?: number;\n108: }): PublicThresholds {\n109:   const resolved = resolveAdvisorThresholdConfig(args);\n110:   return {\n111:     confidenceThreshold: resolved.confidenceThreshold,\n112:     uncertaintyThreshold: resolved.uncertaintyThreshold,\n113:     confidenceOnly: resolved.confidenceOnly,\n114:   };\n115: }\n116: \n117: function runtimeLaneHealthForStatus(status: AdvisorStatus): AdvisorScoringOptions['runtimeLaneHealth'] | undefined {\n118:   if (status.freshness !== 'stale') {\n119:     return undefined;\n120:   }\n121:   return {\n122:     graph_causal: {\n123:       status: 'runtime_degraded',\n124:       reason: status.trustState.reason ?? 'skill_graph_stale',\n125:     },\n126:   };\n127: }\n128: \n129: function renderableStatus(status: AdvisorStatus): AdvisorStatus {\n130:   const trustState = status.trustState.state;\n131:   if (status.freshness === 'unavailable' && (trustState === 'live' || trustState === 'stale')) {\n132:     return { ...status, freshness: trustState };\n133:   }\n134:   return status;\n135: }\n136: \n137: function emptyOutput(args: {\n138:   workspaceRoot: string;\n139:   effectiveThresholds: AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'];\n140:   freshness: AdvisorRecommendOutput['freshness'];\n141:   trustState: AdvisorRecommendOutput['trustState'];\n142:   warnings?: readonly string[];\n143:   abstainReasons?: readonly string[];\n144: }): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n145:   return AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse({\n146:     workspaceRoot: args.workspaceRoot,\n147:     effectiveThresholds: args.effectiveThresholds,\n148:     recommendations: [],\n149:     ambiguous: false,\n150:     freshness: args.freshness,\n151:     trustState: args.trustState,\n152:     generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n153:     cache: {\n154:       hit: false,\n155:       sourceSignaturePresent: false,\n156:     },\n157:     ...(args.warnings && args.warnings.length > 0 ? { warnings: [...args.warnings] } : {}),\n158:     ...(args.abstainReasons && args.abstainReasons.length > 0 ? { abstainReasons: [...args.abstainReasons] } : {}),\n159:   });\n160: }\n161: \n162: // The canonical flag is checked first so the reason names it when both are set.\n163: const ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS = [\n164:   'SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED',\n165:   'SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED',\n166: ] as const;\n167: \n168: function disabledOutput(\n169:   workspaceRoot: string,\n170:   effectiveThresholds: PublicThresholds,\n171:   disabledBy: string,\n172: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n173:   return emptyOutput({\n174:     workspaceRoot,\n175:     effectiveThresholds,\n176:     freshness: 'unavailable',\n177:     trustState: unavailableTrustState('ADVISOR_DISABLED'),\n178:     warnings: ['ADVISOR_DISABLED'],\n179:     abstainReasons: [`Skill advisor disabled by ${disabledBy}.`],\n180:   });\n181: }\n182: \n183: function absentOutput(\n184:   status: AdvisorStatus,\n185:   workspaceRoot: string,\n186:   effectiveThresholds: AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'],\n187: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n188:   return emptyOutput({\n189:     workspaceRoot,\n190:     effectiveThresholds,\n191:     freshness: 'absent',\n192:     trustState: status.trustState,\n193:     warnings: [status.trustState.reason ?? 'ADVISOR_FRESHNESS_ABSENT'],\n194:     abstainReasons: ['Skill advisor freshness is absent; returning fail-open empty recommendations.'],\n195:   });\n196: }\n197: \n198: function unavailableOutput(\n199:   status: AdvisorStatus,\n200:   workspaceRoot: string,\n201:   effectiveThresholds: AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'],\n202: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n203:   return emptyOutput({\n204:     workspaceRoot,\n205:     effectiveThresholds,\n206:     freshness: 'unavailable',\n207:     trustState: {\n208:       ...status.trustState,\n209:       state: 'unavailable',\n210:       reason: 'advisor_unavailable',\n211:     },\n212:     warnings: ['advisor_unavailable', ...(status.errors ?? [])],\n213:     abstainReasons: ['Skill advisor freshness is unavailable; returning fail-open empty recommendations.'],\n214:   });\n215: }\n216: \n217: function safeMany(values: readonly string[] | undefined): string[] {\n218:   return (values ?? [])\n219:     .map((value) => sanitizeSkillLabel(value))\n220:     .filter((value): value is string => Boolean(value));\n221: }\n222: \n223: function evidenceFeature(value: string): string {\n224:   const prefix = value.split(':', 1)[0];\n225:   switch (prefix) {\n226:     case 'phrase':\n227:       return 'phrase_match';\n228:     case 'token':\n229:       return 'token_match';\n230:     case 'hint':\n231:       return 'category_hint';\n232:     case 'derived':\n233:       return 'derived_skill_signal';\n234:     case 'doc':\n235:       return 'doc_reference_signal';\n236:     case 'cosine':\n237:       return 'semantic_similarity';\n238:     default:\n239:       if (value.includes('disambiguation')) return 'disambiguation_rule';\n240:       if (value.includes('surface')) return 'surface_signal';\n241:       if (value.includes('intent')) return 'intent_signal';\n242:       if (value.includes('loop')) return 'workflow_signal';\n243:       return 'scorer_signal';\n244:   }\n245: }\n246: \n247: function publicWhyRecommended(recommendation: ScoredRecommendation) {\n248:   const positiveLanes = recommendation.laneContributions\n249:     .filter((lane) => lane.rawScore > 0 || lane.weightedScore > 0)\n250:     .sort((left, right) => right.weightedScore - left.weightedScore)\n251:     .slice(0, 4);\n252:   const matchedSkillFeatures = positiveLanes.flatMap((lane) => (\n253:     Array.from(new Set(lane.evidence.map((entry) => evidenceFeature(entry)))).map((feature) => ({\n254:       lane: lane.lane,\n255:       feature,\n256:     }))\n257:   ));\n258:   const dominant = recommendation.dominantLane;\n259:   return {\n260:     reason: dominant\n261:       ? `Recommended from ranker signals: ${dominant} contributed the strongest live score.`\n262:       : 'Recommended from ranker signals without a single dominant live lane.',\n263:     dominantLane: dominant,\n264:     topLanes: positiveLanes.map((lane) => ({\n265:       lane: lane.lane,\n266:       rawScore: lane.rawScore,\n267:       weightedScore: lane.weightedScore,\n268:       weight: lane.weight,\n269:       shadowOnly: lane.shadowOnly,\n270:       evidenceTypes: Array.from(new Set(lane.evidence.map((entry) => evidenceFeature(entry)))),\n271:       evidenceCount: lane.evidence.length,\n272:     })),\n273:     matchedSkillFeatures,\n274:   };\n275: }\n276: \n277: // Doc evidence entries are skill-relative markdown paths emitted by the\n278: // derived lane as `doc:<path>`. The allowlist rejects anything that\n279: // could smuggle prompt content or path traversal into the response.\n280: const SAFE_DOC_PATH = /^(references|assets)\\/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.md$/;\n281: \n282: export function matchedDocsFromContributions(\n283:   recommendation: { readonly laneContributions: ReadonlyArray<{ readonly evidence: readonly string[] }> },\n284: ): string[] {\n285:   const docs: string[] = [];\n286:   for (const lane of recommendation.laneContributions) {\n287:     for (const entry of lane.evidence) {\n288:       if (!entry.startsWith('doc:')) continue;\n289:       const path = entry.slice(4);\n290:       if (!SAFE_DOC_PATH.test(path) || path.includes('..')) continue;\n291:       if (!docs.includes(path)) docs.push(path);\n292:       if (docs.length >= 3) return docs;\n293:     }\n294:   }\n295:   return docs;\n296: }\n297: \n298: function workflowModeForRecommendation(\n299:   recommendation: ScoredRecommendation,\n300:   prompt: string,\n301: ): string | undefined {\n302:   const directMode = modeForAlias(recommendation.skill);\n303:   const promptMode = recommendation.skill === MERGED_DEEP_SKILL_ID\n304:     ? modeForPromptAlias(prompt)\n305:     : null;\n306:   const workflowMode = sanitizeSkillLabel(directMode ?? promptMode ?? '');\n307:   return workflowMode || undefined;\n308: }\n309: \n310: function publicRecommendation(\n311:   recommendation: ScoredRecommendation,\n312:   includeAttribution: boolean,\n313:   prompt: string,\n314: ) {\n315:   const skillId = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.skill);\n316:   if (!skillId) return null;\n317:   const commandRow = commandRowFor(recommendation.skill);\n318:   const matchedDocs = matchedDocsFromContributions(recommendation);\n319:   const redirectFrom = safeMany(recommendation.redirectFrom);\n320:   const redirectTo = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.redirectTo ?? '');\n321:   const heldBelow = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.heldBelow ?? '');\n322:   const sanitizedStatus = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.lifecycleStatus);\n323:   const status: PublicRecommendationStatus | undefined = sanitizedStatus === 'active'\n324:     || sanitizedStatus === 'deprecated'\n325:     || sanitizedStatus === 'archived'\n326:     || sanitizedStatus === 'future'\n327:     ? sanitizedStatus as PublicRecommendationStatus\n328:     : undefined;\n329:   const workflowMode = workflowModeForRecommendation(recommendation, prompt);\n330:   return {\n331:     skillId,\n332:     kind: recommendation.kind,\n333:     score: recommendation.score,\n334:     confidence: recommendation.confidence,\n335:     uncertainty: recommendation.uncertainty,\n336:     dominantLane: recommendation.dominantLane,\n337:     ...(includeAttribution ? {\n338:       laneBreakdown: recommendation.laneContributions.map((lane) => ({\n339:         lane: lane.lane,\n340:         rawScore: lane.rawScore,\n341:         weightedScore: lane.weightedScore,\n342:         weight: lane.weight,\n343:         shadowOnly: lane.shadowOnly,\n344:       })),\n345:       why_recommended: publicWhyRecommended(recommendation),\n346:     } : {}),\n347:     ...(matchedDocs.length > 0 ? { matchedDocs } : {}),\n348:     ...(redirectFrom.length > 0 ? { redirectFrom } : {}),\n349:     ...(redirectTo ? { redirectTo } : {}),\n350:     // Hook briefs re-derive ambiguity from the public list, so a skill the typed\n351:     // command already ranked below its seed has to say so here.\n352:     ...(heldBelow ? { heldBelow } : {}),\n353:     ...(status ? { status } : {}),\n354:     ...(workflowMode ? { workflowMode } : {}),\n355:     // A command row is the contract a reader acts on, so its runnable string,\n356:     // policy and owner travel with the pick. An id with no row adds nothing.\n357:     ...(commandRow ? {\n358:       command: commandRow.command,\n359:       ...(commandRow.policy ? { policy: commandRow.policy } : {}),\n360:       ownerSkillId: commandRow.ownerSkillId,\n361:     } : {}),\n362:   };\n363: }\n364: \n365: // The front door runs from the request's workspaceRoot, and a caller may name\n366: // another checkout there, such as a worktree under the repository root. Its copy\n367: // can predate --prompt-stdin and would resolve an empty prompt, so such a copy\n368: // gets no compiled route rather than the prompt in argv.\n369: export function frontDoorReadsPromptFromStdin(frontDoorPath: string): boolean {\n370:   try {\n371:     return readFileSync(frontDoorPath, 'utf8').includes('--prompt-stdin');\n372:   } catch {\n373:     return false;\n374:   }\n375: }\n376: \n377: function compiledRouteForRecommendation(\n378:   skillId: string,\n379:   prompt: string,\n380:   workspaceRoot: string,\n381:   surfaceHint?: string,\n382: ): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {\n383:   if (!COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS.has(skillId)) return undefined;\n384:   const frontDoor = resolve(workspaceRoot, '.skilled', 'bin', 'compiled-route.cjs');\n385:   if (!frontDoorReadsPromptFromStdin(frontDoor)) {\n386:     emitCompiledRoutingBreadcrumb(`compiled-route front door cannot read the prompt from stdin; skipping hub=${skillId}`);\n387:     return undefined;\n388:   }\n389:   try {\n390:     const args = [\n391:       frontDoor,\n392:       '--hub',\n393:       skillId,\n394:       '--prompt-stdin',\n395:     ];\n396:     // A hint the caller already holds is forwarded as its own argv element;\n397:     // the front door ignores a value that names no known surface.\n398:     if (surfaceHint) args.push('--surface-hint', surfaceHint);\n399:     const output = execFileSync(process.execPath, args, {\n400:       cwd: workspaceRoot,\n401:       encoding: 'utf8',\n402:       input: prompt,\n403:       stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n404:       timeout: 5_000,\n405:       maxBuffer: 1_048_576,\n406:     });\n407:     const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(output.trim());\n408:     if (typeof parsed !== 'object' || parsed === null || Array.isArray(parsed)) {\n409:       return undefined;\n410:     }\n411:     const compiledRoute = parsed as Record<string, unknown>;\n412:     return compiledRoute.servingAuthority === 'legacy' ? undefined : compiledRoute;\n413:   } catch (error) {\n414:     // Surface the otherwise-silent fallback (debug-gated), including any child\n415:     // stderr the pipe above now captures instead of discarding. The served\n416:     // outcome is unchanged: a failed probe attaches no compiled route (legacy).\n417:     const childStderr = (error as { stderr?: unknown } | null)?.stderr;\n418:     const detail = typeof childStderr === 'string' && childStderr.trim()\n419:       ? ` child-stderr=${childStderr.trim()}`\n420:       : '';\n421:     emitCompiledRoutingBreadcrumb(\n422:       `compiled-route subprocess failed for hub=${skillId}: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}${detail}`,\n423:     );\n424:     return undefined;\n425:   }\n426: }\n427: \n428: function enrichCompiledRoutes(\n429:   output: AdvisorRecommendOutput,\n430:   prompt: string,\n431:   workspaceRoot: string,\n432:   surfaceHint?: string,\n433:   topOnly = false,\n434: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n435:   const mode = parseCompiledRoutingFlagMode(process.env.SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING);\n436:   if (mode === 'invalid') {\n437:     emitCompiledRoutingBreadcrumb(\n438:       `ignoring invalid SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=${JSON.stringify(process.env.SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING)}; serving legacy`,\n439:     );\n440:   }\n441:   // Only enrich hubs the flag permits. The default cohort now covers all 7\n442:   // compiled-eligible hubs (mirrors the runtime resolver's own default-on\n443:   // cohort), so unset attaches compiledRoute for those hubs; the kill-switch\n444:   // ('0'|'false'|'off') and invalid values still skip enrichment for every hub.\n445:   // Skip the schema re-parse entirely when nothing is eligible so the output is\n446:   // returned unchanged.\n447:   const anyEligible = output.recommendations.some((r) => compiledRoutingEnabledForHub(r.skillId));\n448:   if (!anyEligible) return output;\n449:   // A command row that already ranks in this result offers its command by itself,\n450:   // so the owning hub must not offer the same one again and spend a second slot on it.\n451:   const alreadyOffered = new Set<string>();\n452:   for (const recommendation of output.recommendations) {\n453:     if (recommendation.command) alreadyOffered.add(recommendation.command);\n454:   }\n455:   return AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse({\n456:     ...output,\n457:     recommendations: output.recommendations.map((recommendation, index) => {\n458:       // Each lookup is a subprocess, so a caller that acts on the top pick alone\n459:       // pays for that one and no more.\n460:       if (topOnly && index > 0) return recommendation;\n461:       if (!compiledRoutingEnabledForHub(recommendation.skillId)) return recommendation;\n462:       const compiledRoute = compiledRouteForRecommendation(\n463:         recommendation.skillId,\n464:         prompt,\n465:         workspaceRoot,\n466:         surfaceHint,\n467:       );\n468:       if (!compiledRoute) return recommendation;\n469:       // The route answers which mode the hub would take; the command is what a reader\n470:       // types to run it, so it rides along only when the route names exactly one mode\n471:       // that has a command. A broader route leaves the key off rather than guessing.\n472:       const command = attachCommand(recommendation.skillId, compiledRoute, prompt);\n473:       return command && !alreadyOffered.has(command)\n474:         ? {\n475:           ...recommendation,\n476:           compiledRoute,\n477:           command,\n478:           ...(Object.hasOwn(COMMAND_POLICIES, command) ? { policy: COMMAND_POLICIES[command] } : {}),\n479:         }\n480:         : { ...recommendation, compiledRoute };\n481:     }),\n482:   });\n483: }\n484: \n485: // A typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode: the\n486: // reader already named the command, and a compiled route only guesses which mode\n487: // they meant. The top recommendation carries it because that is the row a reader\n488: // acts on, and an unrelated top keeps the output it had.\n489: export function attachTypedCommand(\n490:   output: AdvisorRecommendOutput,\n491:   prompt: string,\n492: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n493:   const top = output.recommendations[0];\n494:   if (!top) return output;\n495:   const typed = typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt);\n496:   if (!typed) return output;\n497:   return AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse({\n498:     ...output,\n499:     recommendations: [\n500:       {\n501:         ...top,\n502:         command: typed.command,\n503:         policy: typed.policy,\n504:         ownerSkillId: typed.ownerSkillId,\n505:       },\n506:       ...output.recommendations.slice(1),\n507:     ],\n508:   });\n509: }\n510: \n511: function publicShadowRecommendations(recommendations: readonly ScoredRecommendation[], topK: number): ShadowRecommendation[] {\n512:   const shadowRecommendations: ShadowRecommendation[] = [];\n513:   for (const recommendation of recommendations) {\n514:     const skillId = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.skill);\n515:     if (!skillId) continue;\n516:     const shadowContributions = recommendation.laneContributions.map((lane) => ({\n517:       lane: lane.lane,\n518:       weightedScore: lane.rawScore * DEFAULT_SHADOW_SCORER_LANE_WEIGHTS[lane.lane],\n519:     }));\n520:     const shadowScore = roundScore(shadowContributions.reduce((total, lane) => total + lane.weightedScore, 0));\n521:     const dominant = shadowContributions\n522:       .filter((lane) => lane.weightedScore > 0)\n523:       .sort((left, right) => right.weightedScore - left.weightedScore)[0]?.lane ?? null;\n524:     shadowRecommendations.push({\n525:         skillId,\n526:         liveScore: recommendation.score,\n527:         shadowScore,\n528:         delta: roundScore(shadowScore - recommendation.score),\n529:         dominantShadowLane: dominant,\n530:     });\n531:   }\n532:   return shadowRecommendations\n533:     .sort((left, right) => right.shadowScore - left.shadowScore || left.skillId.localeCompare(right.skillId))\n534:     .slice(0, topK);\n535: }\n536: \n537: function roundScore(value: number): number {\n538:   return Math.round(value * 1_000_000) / 1_000_000;\n539: }\n540: \n541: // A semantic lane that fell back to phrase scoring still answers, so the reason\n542: // it declined travels as a warning rather than changing the recommendation.\n543: export function semanticLaneOffWarning(reason: string | null): string[] {\n544:   return reason ? [`semantic_lane_off:${reason}`] : [];\n545: }\n546: \n547: function outputWarnings(\n548:   status: AdvisorStatus,\n549:   result: ReturnType<typeof scoreAdvisorPrompt>,\n550:   semanticLaneOffReason: string | null,\n551: ): string[] {\n552:   const degradedLanes = result.metrics.degradedLanes ?? [];\n553:   return [\n554:     ...(status.freshness === 'stale' ? [status.trustState.reason ?? 'STALE_ADVISOR_FRESHNESS'] : []),\n555:     ...(degradedLanes.length > 0\n556:       ? [`runtime_degraded_lanes:${degradedLanes.join(',')}`]\n557:       : []),\n558:     ...semanticLaneOffWarning(semanticLaneOffReason),\n559:   ];\n560: }\n561: \n562: function outputAbstainReasons(\n563:   input: AdvisorRecommendInput,\n564:   result: ReturnType<typeof scoreAdvisorPrompt>,\n565: ): string[] {\n566:   if (!input.options?.includeAbstainReasons) return [];\n567:   return [\n568:     ...(result.unknown ? ['No recommendation passed confidence and uncertainty thresholds.'] : []),\n569:     ...(result.abstainReasons ?? []),\n570:   ];\n571: }\n572: \n573: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n574: // 4. CORE LOGIC\n575: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n576: \n577: async function computeRecommendationOutput(input: AdvisorRecommendInput): Promise<AdvisorRecommendOutput> {\n578:   // Canonicalize via realpath after the schema allowlist check.\n579:   const workspaceRoot = input.workspaceRoot\n580:     ? canonicalizeWorkspaceRoot(input.workspaceRoot)\n581:     : findWorkspaceRoot();\n582:   const effectiveThresholds = publicThresholds({\n583:     confidenceThreshold: input.options?.confidenceThreshold,\n584:     uncertaintyThreshold: input.options?.uncertaintyThreshold,\n585:   });\n586:   // Detect on-disk corruption here too: without it a malformed artifact reads\n587:   // 'live' from the generation counters and the recommend path would serve\n588:   // results as fresh. The verdict is cached per generation, so the quick_check\n589:   // runs at most once per rebuild rather than on every recommendation.\n590:   const status = renderableStatus(readAdvisorStatus({ workspaceRoot, checkArtifactIntegrity: true }));\n591:   if (status.freshness === 'unavailable') {\n592:     return unavailableOutput(status, workspaceRoot, effectiveThresholds);\n593:   }\n594:   if (status.freshness === 'absent') {\n595:     return absentOutput(status, workspaceRoot, effectiveThresholds);\n596:   }\n597:   const sourceSignature = cacheSourceSignature(status);\n598:   advisorPromptCache.invalidateSourceSignatureChange(sourceSignature);\n599:   const key = advisorPromptCache.makeKey({\n600:     canonicalPrompt: input.prompt.trim(),\n601:     sourceSignature,\n602:     workspaceRoot,\n603:     runtime: 'mcp',\n604:     maxTokens: input.options?.topK,\n605:     thresholdConfig: {\n606:       confidenceThreshold: input.options?.confidenceThreshold,\n607:       uncertaintyThreshold: input.options?.uncertaintyThreshold,\n608:       includeAttribution: input.options?.includeAttribution,\n609:       includeAbstainReasons: input.options?.includeAbstainReasons,\n610:     },\n611:   });\n612:   const cached = advisorPromptCache.get(key);\n613:   if (cached) {\n614:     const cachedOutput = cached.value as AdvisorRecommendOutput;\n615:     const parsedCachedOutput = AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse({\n616:       ...cachedOutput,\n617:       workspaceRoot,\n618:       effectiveThresholds,\n619:       cache: {\n620:         ...cachedOutput.cache,\n621:         hit: true,\n622:       },\n623:     });\n624:     return attachTypedCommand(\n625:       input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false\n626:         ? parsedCachedOutput\n627:         : enrichCompiledRoutes(parsedCachedOutput, input.prompt, workspaceRoot, input.options?.surfaceHint, input.options?.compiledRouteTopOnly === true),\n628:       input.prompt,\n629:     );\n630:   }\n631: \n632:   const topK = input.options?.topK ?? 3;\n633:   const result = await withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding(input.prompt, () => scoreAdvisorPrompt(input.prompt, {\n634:     workspaceRoot,\n635:     confidenceThreshold: input.options?.confidenceThreshold,\n636:     uncertaintyThreshold: input.options?.uncertaintyThreshold,\n637:     runtimeLaneHealth: runtimeLaneHealthForStatus(status),\n638:   }));\n639:   // The lane records its health while the scored call runs, so the reason is\n640:   // read right after that call settles to describe this call's own fallback.\n641:   const semanticLaneOffReason = getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth().disabledReason;\n642:   const recommendations = result.recommendations\n643:     .map((recommendation) => publicRecommendation(\n644:       recommendation,\n645:       Boolean(input.options?.includeAttribution),\n646:       input.prompt,\n647:     ))\n648:     .filter((recommendation): recommendation is NonNullable<typeof recommendation> => Boolean(recommendation))\n649:     .slice(0, topK);\n650:   const degradedLanes = result.metrics.degradedLanes ?? [];\n651:   const warnings = outputWarnings(status, result, semanticLaneOffReason);\n652:   const abstainReasons = outputAbstainReasons(input, result);\n653:   const output: AdvisorRecommendOutput = {\n654:     workspaceRoot,\n655:     effectiveThresholds,\n656:     recommendations,\n657:     ambiguous: result.ambiguous,\n658:     freshness: status.freshness,\n659:     trustState: status.trustState,\n660:     generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n661:     cache: {\n662:       hit: false,\n663:       sourceSignaturePresent: status.generation > 0 || status.lastGenerationBump !== null,\n664:     },\n665:     _shadow: {\n666:       model: 'advisor-shadow-learned-weights-v1',\n667:       liveWeightsFrozen: true,\n668:       recommendations: publicShadowRecommendations(result.recommendations, topK),\n669:     },\n670:     ...(degradedLanes.length > 0 ? {\n671:       runtimeLaneHealth: {\n672:         liveLaneCount: result.metrics.liveLaneCount,\n673:         degradedLanes: [...degradedLanes],\n674:       },\n675:     } : {}),\n676:     ...(warnings.length > 0 ? { warnings } : {}),\n677:     ...(abstainReasons.length > 0 ? { abstainReasons } : {}),\n678:   };\n679:   const parsed = AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse(output);\n680:   if (shadowDeltaSinkEnabled()) {\n681:     for (const shadow of parsed._shadow?.recommendations ?? []) {\n682:       recordShadowDelta({\n683:         prompt: `hmac:${key}`,\n684:         recommendation: shadow.skillId,\n685:         liveScore: shadow.liveScore,\n686:         shadowScore: shadow.shadowScore,\n687:         delta: shadow.delta,\n688:         dominantLane: shadow.dominantShadowLane,\n689:         timestamp: parsed.generatedAt,\n690:       });\n691:     }\n692:   }\n693:   advisorPromptCache.set({\n694:     key,\n695:     sourceSignature,\n696:     value: parsed,\n697:     skillLabels: recommendationLabels(parsed),\n698:   });\n699:   return attachTypedCommand(\n700:     input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false\n701:       ? parsed\n702:       : enrichCompiledRoutes(parsed, input.prompt, workspaceRoot, input.options?.surfaceHint, input.options?.compiledRouteTopOnly === true),\n703:     input.prompt,\n704:   );\n705: }\n706: \n707: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n708: // 5. EXPORTS\n709: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n710: \n711: export async function handleAdvisorRecommend(args: unknown): Promise<HandlerResponse> {\n712:   const input = AdvisorRecommendInputSchema.parse(args);\n713:   // Canonicalize via realpath after the schema allowlist check.\n714:   const workspaceRoot = input.workspaceRoot\n715:     ? canonicalizeWorkspaceRoot(input.workspaceRoot)\n716:     : findWorkspaceRoot();\n717:   const effectiveThresholds = publicThresholds({\n718:     confidenceThreshold: input.options?.confidenceThreshold,\n719:     uncertaintyThreshold: input.options?.uncertaintyThreshold,\n720:   });\n721:   const disabledBy = ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS.find((flag) => process.env[flag] === '1');\n722:   const data = disabledBy\n723:     ? disabledOutput(workspaceRoot, effectiveThresholds, disabledBy)\n724:     : await computeRecommendationOutput(input);\n725:   return {\n726:     content: [{\n727:       type: 'text',\n728:       text: JSON.stringify({ status: 'ok', data }, null, 2),\n729:     }],\n730:   };\n731: }\n732: ","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts, lines 1-732\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: advisor_recommend Handler\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. IMPORTS\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: \n9: import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\n10: import { readFileSync, realpathSync } from 'node:fs';\n11: import { resolve } from 'node:path';\n12: \n13: import { COMMAND_POLICIES, attachCommand, commandRowFor, typedCommandForTop } from '../lib/command-attach.js';\n14: import { advisorPromptCache } from '../lib/prompt-cache.js';\n15: import {\n16:   resolveAdvisorThresholdConfig,\n17: } from '../lib/skill-advisor-brief.js';\n18: import { scoreAdvisorPrompt } from '../lib/scorer/fusion.js';\n19: import {\n20:   DEEP_ROUTING_PROJECTION_HASH,\n21:   MERGED_DEEP_SKILL_ID,\n22:   modeForAlias,\n23:   modeForPromptAlias,\n24: } from '../lib/scorer/aliases.js';\n25: import {\n26:   getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth,\n27:   withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding,\n28: } from '../lib/scorer/lanes/semantic-shadow.js';\n29: import { DEFAULT_SHADOW_SCORER_LANE_WEIGHTS } from '../lib/scorer/lane-registry.js';\n30: import { sanitizeSkillLabel } from '../lib/render.js';\n31: import { recordShadowDelta, shadowDeltaSinkEnabled } from '../lib/shadow/shadow-sink.js';\n32: import { findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot } from '../lib/utils/workspace-root.js';\n33: import {\n34:   AdvisorRecommendInputSchema,\n35:   AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema,\n36:   type AdvisorRecommendInput,\n37:   type AdvisorRecommendOutput,\n38: } from '../schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.js';\n39: import { readAdvisorStatus } from './advisor-status.js';\n40: import {\n41:   COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS,\n42:   compiledRoutingEnabledForHub,\n43:   parseCompiledRoutingFlagMode,\n44: } from '../lib/compiled-routing-flag.js';\n45: import type { AdvisorScoringOptions } from '../lib/scorer/types.js';\n46: \n47: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n48: // 2. TYPE DEFINITIONS\n49: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n50: \n51: type HandlerResponse = { content: Array<{ type: string; text: string }> };\n52: type AdvisorStatus = ReturnType<typeof readAdvisorStatus>;\n53: type ScoredRecommendation = ReturnType<typeof scoreAdvisorPrompt>['recommendations'][number];\n54: type PublicRecommendationStatus = NonNullable<AdvisorRecommendOutput['recommendations'][number]['status']>;\n55: type PublicThresholds = AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'];\n56: type ShadowRecommendation = NonNullable<AdvisorRecommendOutput['_shadow']>['recommendations'][number];\n57: \n58: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n59: // 3. HELPERS\n60: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n61: \n62: // Emit-only, stderr, debug-gated compiled-routing diagnostic. Never written to\n63: // stdout or the tool response, and never changes the recommendation outcome.\n64: function emitCompiledRoutingBreadcrumb(message: string): void {\n65:   if (process.env.SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING_DEBUG) {\n66:     process.stderr.write(`[compiled-routing] ${message}\\n`);\n67:   }\n68: }\n69: \n70: function findWorkspaceRoot(start = process.cwd()): string {\n71:   return findAdvisorWorkspaceRoot(start, { maxDepth: 12 });\n72: }\n73: \n74: // Canonicalize a caller-supplied workspaceRoot via realpath.\n75: // The schema-level allowlist refinement runs against the same canonical\n76: // form, so a caller passing /tmp/symlink-to-repo gets the real path\n77: // post-symlink before downstream code uses it.\n78: function canonicalizeWorkspaceRoot(input: string): string {\n79:   const resolved = resolve(input);\n80:   try {\n81:     return realpathSync.native(resolved);\n82:   } catch {\n83:     return resolved;\n84:   }\n85: }\n86: \n87: function cacheSourceSignature(status: AdvisorStatus): string {\n88:   return `${status.freshness}:${status.generation}:${status.lastGenerationBump ?? 'never'}:${DEEP_ROUTING_PROJECTION_HASH}`;\n89: }\n90: \n91: function recommendationLabels(output: AdvisorRecommendOutput): string[] {\n92:   return output.recommendations.map((recommendation) => recommendation.skillId);\n93: }\n94: \n95: function unavailableTrustState(reason: string): AdvisorRecommendOutput['trustState'] {\n96:   return {\n97:     state: 'unavailable',\n98:     reason,\n99:     generation: 0,\n100:     checkedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n101:     lastLiveAt: null,\n102:   };\n103: }\n104: \n105: function publicThresholds(args: {\n106:   confidenceThreshold?: number;\n107:   uncertaintyThreshold?: number;\n108: }): PublicThresholds {\n109:   const resolved = resolveAdvisorThresholdConfig(args);\n110:   return {\n111:     confidenceThreshold: resolved.confidenceThreshold,\n112:     uncertaintyThreshold: resolved.uncertaintyThreshold,\n113:     confidenceOnly: resolved.confidenceOnly,\n114:   };\n115: }\n116: \n117: function runtimeLaneHealthForStatus(status: AdvisorStatus): AdvisorScoringOptions['runtimeLaneHealth'] | undefined {\n118:   if (status.freshness !== 'stale') {\n119:     return undefined;\n120:   }\n121:   return {\n122:     graph_causal: {\n123:       status: 'runtime_degraded',\n124:       reason: status.trustState.reason ?? 'skill_graph_stale',\n125:     },\n126:   };\n127: }\n128: \n129: function renderableStatus(status: AdvisorStatus): AdvisorStatus {\n130:   const trustState = status.trustState.state;\n131:   if (status.freshness === 'unavailable' && (trustState === 'live' || trustState === 'stale')) {\n132:     return { ...status, freshness: trustState };\n133:   }\n134:   return status;\n135: }\n136: \n137: function emptyOutput(args: {\n138:   workspaceRoot: string;\n139:   effectiveThresholds: AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'];\n140:   freshness: AdvisorRecommendOutput['freshness'];\n141:   trustState: AdvisorRecommendOutput['trustState'];\n142:   warnings?: readonly string[];\n143:   abstainReasons?: readonly string[];\n144: }): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n145:   return AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse({\n146:     workspaceRoot: args.workspaceRoot,\n147:     effectiveThresholds: args.effectiveThresholds,\n148:     recommendations: [],\n149:     ambiguous: false,\n150:     freshness: args.freshness,\n151:     trustState: args.trustState,\n152:     generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n153:     cache: {\n154:       hit: false,\n155:       sourceSignaturePresent: false,\n156:     },\n157:     ...(args.warnings && args.warnings.length > 0 ? { warnings: [...args.warnings] } : {}),\n158:     ...(args.abstainReasons && args.abstainReasons.length > 0 ? { abstainReasons: [...args.abstainReasons] } : {}),\n159:   });\n160: }\n161: \n162: // The canonical flag is checked first so the reason names it when both are set.\n163: const ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS = [\n164:   'SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED',\n165:   'SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED',\n166: ] as const;\n167: \n168: function disabledOutput(\n169:   workspaceRoot: string,\n170:   effectiveThresholds: PublicThresholds,\n171:   disabledBy: string,\n172: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n173:   return emptyOutput({\n174:     workspaceRoot,\n175:     effectiveThresholds,\n176:     freshness: 'unavailable',\n177:     trustState: unavailableTrustState('ADVISOR_DISABLED'),\n178:     warnings: ['ADVISOR_DISABLED'],\n179:     abstainReasons: [`Skill advisor disabled by ${disabledBy}.`],\n180:   });\n181: }\n182: \n183: function absentOutput(\n184:   status: AdvisorStatus,\n185:   workspaceRoot: string,\n186:   effectiveThresholds: AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'],\n187: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n188:   return emptyOutput({\n189:     workspaceRoot,\n190:     effectiveThresholds,\n191:     freshness: 'absent',\n192:     trustState: status.trustState,\n193:     warnings: [status.trustState.reason ?? 'ADVISOR_FRESHNESS_ABSENT'],\n194:     abstainReasons: ['Skill advisor freshness is absent; returning fail-open empty recommendations.'],\n195:   });\n196: }\n197: \n198: function unavailableOutput(\n199:   status: AdvisorStatus,\n200:   workspaceRoot: string,\n201:   effectiveThresholds: AdvisorRecommendOutput['effectiveThresholds'],\n202: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n203:   return emptyOutput({\n204:     workspaceRoot,\n205:     effectiveThresholds,\n206:     freshness: 'unavailable',\n207:     trustState: {\n208:       ...status.trustState,\n209:       state: 'unavailable',\n210:       reason: 'advisor_unavailable',\n211:     },\n212:     warnings: ['advisor_unavailable', ...(status.errors ?? [])],\n213:     abstainReasons: ['Skill advisor freshness is unavailable; returning fail-open empty recommendations.'],\n214:   });\n215: }\n216: \n217: function safeMany(values: readonly string[] | undefined): string[] {\n218:   return (values ?? [])\n219:     .map((value) => sanitizeSkillLabel(value))\n220:     .filter((value): value is string => Boolean(value));\n221: }\n222: \n223: function evidenceFeature(value: string): string {\n224:   const prefix = value.split(':', 1)[0];\n225:   switch (prefix) {\n226:     case 'phrase':\n227:       return 'phrase_match';\n228:     case 'token':\n229:       return 'token_match';\n230:     case 'hint':\n231:       return 'category_hint';\n232:     case 'derived':\n233:       return 'derived_skill_signal';\n234:     case 'doc':\n235:       return 'doc_reference_signal';\n236:     case 'cosine':\n237:       return 'semantic_similarity';\n238:     default:\n239:       if (value.includes('disambiguation')) return 'disambiguation_rule';\n240:       if (value.includes('surface')) return 'surface_signal';\n241:       if (value.includes('intent')) return 'intent_signal';\n242:       if (value.includes('loop')) return 'workflow_signal';\n243:       return 'scorer_signal';\n244:   }\n245: }\n246: \n247: function publicWhyRecommended(recommendation: ScoredRecommendation) {\n248:   const positiveLanes = recommendation.laneContributions\n249:     .filter((lane) => lane.rawScore > 0 || lane.weightedScore > 0)\n250:     .sort((left, right) => right.weightedScore - left.weightedScore)\n251:     .slice(0, 4);\n252:   const matchedSkillFeatures = positiveLanes.flatMap((lane) => (\n253:     Array.from(new Set(lane.evidence.map((entry) => evidenceFeature(entry)))).map((feature) => ({\n254:       lane: lane.lane,\n255:       feature,\n256:     }))\n257:   ));\n258:   const dominant = recommendation.dominantLane;\n259:   return {\n260:     reason: dominant\n261:       ? `Recommended from ranker signals: ${dominant} contributed the strongest live score.`\n262:       : 'Recommended from ranker signals without a single dominant live lane.',\n263:     dominantLane: dominant,\n264:     topLanes: positiveLanes.map((lane) => ({\n265:       lane: lane.lane,\n266:       rawScore: lane.rawScore,\n267:       weightedScore: lane.weightedScore,\n268:       weight: lane.weight,\n269:       shadowOnly: lane.shadowOnly,\n270:       evidenceTypes: Array.from(new Set(lane.evidence.map((entry) => evidenceFeature(entry)))),\n271:       evidenceCount: lane.evidence.length,\n272:     })),\n273:     matchedSkillFeatures,\n274:   };\n275: }\n276: \n277: // Doc evidence entries are skill-relative markdown paths emitted by the\n278: // derived lane as `doc:<path>`. The allowlist rejects anything that\n279: // could smuggle prompt content or path traversal into the response.\n280: const SAFE_DOC_PATH = /^(references|assets)\\/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+\\.md$/;\n281: \n282: export function matchedDocsFromContributions(\n283:   recommendation: { readonly laneContributions: ReadonlyArray<{ readonly evidence: readonly string[] }> },\n284: ): string[] {\n285:   const docs: string[] = [];\n286:   for (const lane of recommendation.laneContributions) {\n287:     for (const entry of lane.evidence) {\n288:       if (!entry.startsWith('doc:')) continue;\n289:       const path = entry.slice(4);\n290:       if (!SAFE_DOC_PATH.test(path) || path.includes('..')) continue;\n291:       if (!docs.includes(path)) docs.push(path);\n292:       if (docs.length >= 3) return docs;\n293:     }\n294:   }\n295:   return docs;\n296: }\n297: \n298: function workflowModeForRecommendation(\n299:   recommendation: ScoredRecommendation,\n300:   prompt: string,\n301: ): string | undefined {\n302:   const directMode = modeForAlias(recommendation.skill);\n303:   const promptMode = recommendation.skill === MERGED_DEEP_SKILL_ID\n304:     ? modeForPromptAlias(prompt)\n305:     : null;\n306:   const workflowMode = sanitizeSkillLabel(directMode ?? promptMode ?? '');\n307:   return workflowMode || undefined;\n308: }\n309: \n310: function publicRecommendation(\n311:   recommendation: ScoredRecommendation,\n312:   includeAttribution: boolean,\n313:   prompt: string,\n314: ) {\n315:   const skillId = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.skill);\n316:   if (!skillId) return null;\n317:   const commandRow = commandRowFor(recommendation.skill);\n318:   const matchedDocs = matchedDocsFromContributions(recommendation);\n319:   const redirectFrom = safeMany(recommendation.redirectFrom);\n320:   const redirectTo = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.redirectTo ?? '');\n321:   const heldBelow = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.heldBelow ?? '');\n322:   const sanitizedStatus = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.lifecycleStatus);\n323:   const status: PublicRecommendationStatus | undefined = sanitizedStatus === 'active'\n324:     || sanitizedStatus === 'deprecated'\n325:     || sanitizedStatus === 'archived'\n326:     || sanitizedStatus === 'future'\n327:     ? sanitizedStatus as PublicRecommendationStatus\n328:     : undefined;\n329:   const workflowMode = workflowModeForRecommendation(recommendation, prompt);\n330:   return {\n331:     skillId,\n332:     kind: recommendation.kind,\n333:     score: recommendation.score,\n334:     confidence: recommendation.confidence,\n335:     uncertainty: recommendation.uncertainty,\n336:     dominantLane: recommendation.dominantLane,\n337:     ...(includeAttribution ? {\n338:       laneBreakdown: recommendation.laneContributions.map((lane) => ({\n339:         lane: lane.lane,\n340:         rawScore: lane.rawScore,\n341:         weightedScore: lane.weightedScore,\n342:         weight: lane.weight,\n343:         shadowOnly: lane.shadowOnly,\n344:       })),\n345:       why_recommended: publicWhyRecommended(recommendation),\n346:     } : {}),\n347:     ...(matchedDocs.length > 0 ? { matchedDocs } : {}),\n348:     ...(redirectFrom.length > 0 ? { redirectFrom } : {}),\n349:     ...(redirectTo ? { redirectTo } : {}),\n350:     // Hook briefs re-derive ambiguity from the public list, so a skill the typed\n351:     // command already ranked below its seed has to say so here.\n352:     ...(heldBelow ? { heldBelow } : {}),\n353:     ...(status ? { status } : {}),\n354:     ...(workflowMode ? { workflowMode } : {}),\n355:     // A command row is the contract a reader acts on, so its runnable string,\n356:     // policy and owner travel with the pick. An id with no row adds nothing.\n357:     ...(commandRow ? {\n358:       command: commandRow.command,\n359:       ...(commandRow.policy ? { policy: commandRow.policy } : {}),\n360:       ownerSkillId: commandRow.ownerSkillId,\n361:     } : {}),\n362:   };\n363: }\n364: \n365: // The front door runs from the request's workspaceRoot, and a caller may name\n366: // another checkout there, such as a worktree under the repository root. Its copy\n367: // can predate --prompt-stdin and would resolve an empty prompt, so such a copy\n368: // gets no compiled route rather than the prompt in argv.\n369: export function frontDoorReadsPromptFromStdin(frontDoorPath: string): boolean {\n370:   try {\n371:     return readFileSync(frontDoorPath, 'utf8').includes('--prompt-stdin');\n372:   } catch {\n373:     return false;\n374:   }\n375: }\n376: \n377: function compiledRouteForRecommendation(\n378:   skillId: string,\n379:   prompt: string,\n380:   workspaceRoot: string,\n381:   surfaceHint?: string,\n382: ): Record<string, unknown> | undefined {\n383:   if (!COMPILED_ROUTING_HUBS.has(skillId)) return undefined;\n384:   const frontDoor = resolve(workspaceRoot, '.skilled', 'bin', 'compiled-route.cjs');\n385:   if (!frontDoorReadsPromptFromStdin(frontDoor)) {\n386:     emitCompiledRoutingBreadcrumb(`compiled-route front door cannot read the prompt from stdin; skipping hub=${skillId}`);\n387:     return undefined;\n388:   }\n389:   try {\n390:     const args = [\n391:       frontDoor,\n392:       '--hub',\n393:       skillId,\n394:       '--prompt-stdin',\n395:     ];\n396:     // A hint the caller already holds is forwarded as its own argv element;\n397:     // the front door ignores a value that names no known surface.\n398:     if (surfaceHint) args.push('--surface-hint', surfaceHint);\n399:     const output = execFileSync(process.execPath, args, {\n400:       cwd: workspaceRoot,\n401:       encoding: 'utf8',\n402:       input: prompt,\n403:       stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe'],\n404:       timeout: 5_000,\n405:       maxBuffer: 1_048_576,\n406:     });\n407:     const parsed: unknown = JSON.parse(output.trim());\n408:     if (typeof parsed !== 'object' || parsed === null || Array.isArray(parsed)) {\n409:       return undefined;\n410:     }\n411:     const compiledRoute = parsed as Record<string, unknown>;\n412:     return compiledRoute.servingAuthority === 'legacy' ? undefined : compiledRoute;\n413:   } catch (error) {\n414:     // Surface the otherwise-silent fallback (debug-gated), including any child\n415:     // stderr the pipe above now captures instead of discarding. The served\n416:     // outcome is unchanged: a failed probe attaches no compiled route (legacy).\n417:     const childStderr = (error as { stderr?: unknown } | null)?.stderr;\n418:     const detail = typeof childStderr === 'string' && childStderr.trim()\n419:       ? ` child-stderr=${childStderr.trim()}`\n420:       : '';\n421:     emitCompiledRoutingBreadcrumb(\n422:       `compiled-route subprocess failed for hub=${skillId}: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}${detail}`,\n423:     );\n424:     return undefined;\n425:   }\n426: }\n427: \n428: function enrichCompiledRoutes(\n429:   output: AdvisorRecommendOutput,\n430:   prompt: string,\n431:   workspaceRoot: string,\n432:   surfaceHint?: string,\n433:   topOnly = false,\n434: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n435:   const mode = parseCompiledRoutingFlagMode(process.env.SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING);\n436:   if (mode === 'invalid') {\n437:     emitCompiledRoutingBreadcrumb(\n438:       `ignoring invalid SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=${JSON.stringify(process.env.SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING)}; serving legacy`,\n439:     );\n440:   }\n441:   // Only enrich hubs the flag permits. The default cohort now covers all 7\n442:   // compiled-eligible hubs (mirrors the runtime resolver's own default-on\n443:   // cohort), so unset attaches compiledRoute for those hubs; the kill-switch\n444:   // ('0'|'false'|'off') and invalid values still skip enrichment for every hub.\n445:   // Skip the schema re-parse entirely when nothing is eligible so the output is\n446:   // returned unchanged.\n447:   const anyEligible = output.recommendations.some((r) => compiledRoutingEnabledForHub(r.skillId));\n448:   if (!anyEligible) return output;\n449:   // A command row that already ranks in this result offers its command by itself,\n450:   // so the owning hub must not offer the same one again and spend a second slot on it.\n451:   const alreadyOffered = new Set<string>();\n452:   for (const recommendation of output.recommendations) {\n453:     if (recommendation.command) alreadyOffered.add(recommendation.command);\n454:   }\n455:   return AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse({\n456:     ...output,\n457:     recommendations: output.recommendations.map((recommendation, index) => {\n458:       // Each lookup is a subprocess, so a caller that acts on the top pick alone\n459:       // pays for that one and no more.\n460:       if (topOnly && index > 0) return recommendation;\n461:       if (!compiledRoutingEnabledForHub(recommendation.skillId)) return recommendation;\n462:       const compiledRoute = compiledRouteForRecommendation(\n463:         recommendation.skillId,\n464:         prompt,\n465:         workspaceRoot,\n466:         surfaceHint,\n467:       );\n468:       if (!compiledRoute) return recommendation;\n469:       // The route answers which mode the hub would take; the command is what a reader\n470:       // types to run it, so it rides along only when the route names exactly one mode\n471:       // that has a command. A broader route leaves the key off rather than guessing.\n472:       const command = attachCommand(recommendation.skillId, compiledRoute, prompt);\n473:       return command && !alreadyOffered.has(command)\n474:         ? {\n475:           ...recommendation,\n476:           compiledRoute,\n477:           command,\n478:           ...(Object.hasOwn(COMMAND_POLICIES, command) ? { policy: COMMAND_POLICIES[command] } : {}),\n479:         }\n480:         : { ...recommendation, compiledRoute };\n481:     }),\n482:   });\n483: }\n484: \n485: // A typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode: the\n486: // reader already named the command, and a compiled route only guesses which mode\n487: // they meant. The top recommendation carries it because that is the row a reader\n488: // acts on, and an unrelated top keeps the output it had.\n489: export function attachTypedCommand(\n490:   output: AdvisorRecommendOutput,\n491:   prompt: string,\n492: ): AdvisorRecommendOutput {\n493:   const top = output.recommendations[0];\n494:   if (!top) return output;\n495:   const typed = typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt);\n496:   if (!typed) return output;\n497:   return AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse({\n498:     ...output,\n499:     recommendations: [\n500:       {\n501:         ...top,\n502:         command: typed.command,\n503:         policy: typed.policy,\n504:         ownerSkillId: typed.ownerSkillId,\n505:       },\n506:       ...output.recommendations.slice(1),\n507:     ],\n508:   });\n509: }\n510: \n511: function publicShadowRecommendations(recommendations: readonly ScoredRecommendation[], topK: number): ShadowRecommendation[] {\n512:   const shadowRecommendations: ShadowRecommendation[] = [];\n513:   for (const recommendation of recommendations) {\n514:     const skillId = sanitizeSkillLabel(recommendation.skill);\n515:     if (!skillId) continue;\n516:     const shadowContributions = recommendation.laneContributions.map((lane) => ({\n517:       lane: lane.lane,\n518:       weightedScore: lane.rawScore * DEFAULT_SHADOW_SCORER_LANE_WEIGHTS[lane.lane],\n519:     }));\n520:     const shadowScore = roundScore(shadowContributions.reduce((total, lane) => total + lane.weightedScore, 0));\n521:     const dominant = shadowContributions\n522:       .filter((lane) => lane.weightedScore > 0)\n523:       .sort((left, right) => right.weightedScore - left.weightedScore)[0]?.lane ?? null;\n524:     shadowRecommendations.push({\n525:         skillId,\n526:         liveScore: recommendation.score,\n527:         shadowScore,\n528:         delta: roundScore(shadowScore - recommendation.score),\n529:         dominantShadowLane: dominant,\n530:     });\n531:   }\n532:   return shadowRecommendations\n533:     .sort((left, right) => right.shadowScore - left.shadowScore || left.skillId.localeCompare(right.skillId))\n534:     .slice(0, topK);\n535: }\n536: \n537: function roundScore(value: number): number {\n538:   return Math.round(value * 1_000_000) / 1_000_000;\n539: }\n540: \n541: // A semantic lane that fell back to phrase scoring still answers, so the reason\n542: // it declined travels as a warning rather than changing the recommendation.\n543: export function semanticLaneOffWarning(reason: string | null): string[] {\n544:   return reason ? [`semantic_lane_off:${reason}`] : [];\n545: }\n546: \n547: function outputWarnings(\n548:   status: AdvisorStatus,\n549:   result: ReturnType<typeof scoreAdvisorPrompt>,\n550:   semanticLaneOffReason: string | null,\n551: ): string[] {\n552:   const degradedLanes = result.metrics.degradedLanes ?? [];\n553:   return [\n554:     ...(status.freshness === 'stale' ? [status.trustState.reason ?? 'STALE_ADVISOR_FRESHNESS'] : []),\n555:     ...(degradedLanes.length > 0\n556:       ? [`runtime_degraded_lanes:${degradedLanes.join(',')}`]\n557:       : []),\n558:     ...semanticLaneOffWarning(semanticLaneOffReason),\n559:   ];\n560: }\n561: \n562: function outputAbstainReasons(\n563:   input: AdvisorRecommendInput,\n564:   result: ReturnType<typeof scoreAdvisorPrompt>,\n565: ): string[] {\n566:   if (!input.options?.includeAbstainReasons) return [];\n567:   return [\n568:     ...(result.unknown ? ['No recommendation passed confidence and uncertainty thresholds.'] : []),\n569:     ...(result.abstainReasons ?? []),\n570:   ];\n571: }\n572: \n573: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n574: // 4. CORE LOGIC\n575: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n576: \n577: async function computeRecommendationOutput(input: AdvisorRecommendInput): Promise<AdvisorRecommendOutput> {\n578:   // Canonicalize via realpath after the schema allowlist check.\n579:   const workspaceRoot = input.workspaceRoot\n580:     ? canonicalizeWorkspaceRoot(input.workspaceRoot)\n581:     : findWorkspaceRoot();\n582:   const effectiveThresholds = publicThresholds({\n583:     confidenceThreshold: input.options?.confidenceThreshold,\n584:     uncertaintyThreshold: input.options?.uncertaintyThreshold,\n585:   });\n586:   // Detect on-disk corruption here too: without it a malformed artifact reads\n587:   // 'live' from the generation counters and the recommend path would serve\n588:   // results as fresh. The verdict is cached per generation, so the quick_check\n589:   // runs at most once per rebuild rather than on every recommendation.\n590:   const status = renderableStatus(readAdvisorStatus({ workspaceRoot, checkArtifactIntegrity: true }));\n591:   if (status.freshness === 'unavailable') {\n592:     return unavailableOutput(status, workspaceRoot, effectiveThresholds);\n593:   }\n594:   if (status.freshness === 'absent') {\n595:     return absentOutput(status, workspaceRoot, effectiveThresholds);\n596:   }\n597:   const sourceSignature = cacheSourceSignature(status);\n598:   advisorPromptCache.invalidateSourceSignatureChange(sourceSignature);\n599:   const key = advisorPromptCache.makeKey({\n600:     canonicalPrompt: input.prompt.trim(),\n601:     sourceSignature,\n602:     workspaceRoot,\n603:     runtime: 'mcp',\n604:     maxTokens: input.options?.topK,\n605:     thresholdConfig: {\n606:       confidenceThreshold: input.options?.confidenceThreshold,\n607:       uncertaintyThreshold: input.options?.uncertaintyThreshold,\n608:       includeAttribution: input.options?.includeAttribution,\n609:       includeAbstainReasons: input.options?.includeAbstainReasons,\n610:     },\n611:   });\n612:   const cached = advisorPromptCache.get(key);\n613:   if (cached) {\n614:     const cachedOutput = cached.value as AdvisorRecommendOutput;\n615:     const parsedCachedOutput = AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse({\n616:       ...cachedOutput,\n617:       workspaceRoot,\n618:       effectiveThresholds,\n619:       cache: {\n620:         ...cachedOutput.cache,\n621:         hit: true,\n622:       },\n623:     });\n624:     return attachTypedCommand(\n625:       input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false\n626:         ? parsedCachedOutput\n627:         : enrichCompiledRoutes(parsedCachedOutput, input.prompt, workspaceRoot, input.options?.surfaceHint, input.options?.compiledRouteTopOnly === true),\n628:       input.prompt,\n629:     );\n630:   }\n631: \n632:   const topK = input.options?.topK ?? 3;\n633:   const result = await withSemanticShadowPromptEmbedding(input.prompt, () => scoreAdvisorPrompt(input.prompt, {\n634:     workspaceRoot,\n635:     confidenceThreshold: input.options?.confidenceThreshold,\n636:     uncertaintyThreshold: input.options?.uncertaintyThreshold,\n637:     runtimeLaneHealth: runtimeLaneHealthForStatus(status),\n638:   }));\n639:   // The lane records its health while the scored call runs, so the reason is\n640:   // read right after that call settles to describe this call's own fallback.\n641:   const semanticLaneOffReason = getSemanticShadowRuntimeHealth().disabledReason;\n642:   const recommendations = result.recommendations\n643:     .map((recommendation) => publicRecommendation(\n644:       recommendation,\n645:       Boolean(input.options?.includeAttribution),\n646:       input.prompt,\n647:     ))\n648:     .filter((recommendation): recommendation is NonNullable<typeof recommendation> => Boolean(recommendation))\n649:     .slice(0, topK);\n650:   const degradedLanes = result.metrics.degradedLanes ?? [];\n651:   const warnings = outputWarnings(status, result, semanticLaneOffReason);\n652:   const abstainReasons = outputAbstainReasons(input, result);\n653:   const output: AdvisorRecommendOutput = {\n654:     workspaceRoot,\n655:     effectiveThresholds,\n656:     recommendations,\n657:     ambiguous: result.ambiguous,\n658:     freshness: status.freshness,\n659:     trustState: status.trustState,\n660:     generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n661:     cache: {\n662:       hit: false,\n663:       sourceSignaturePresent: status.generation > 0 || status.lastGenerationBump !== null,\n664:     },\n665:     _shadow: {\n666:       model: 'advisor-shadow-learned-weights-v1',\n667:       liveWeightsFrozen: true,\n668:       recommendations: publicShadowRecommendations(result.recommendations, topK),\n669:     },\n670:     ...(degradedLanes.length > 0 ? {\n671:       runtimeLaneHealth: {\n672:         liveLaneCount: result.metrics.liveLaneCount,\n673:         degradedLanes: [...degradedLanes],\n674:       },\n675:     } : {}),\n676:     ...(warnings.length > 0 ? { warnings } : {}),\n677:     ...(abstainReasons.length > 0 ? { abstainReasons } : {}),\n678:   };\n679:   const parsed = AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse(output);\n680:   if (shadowDeltaSinkEnabled()) {\n681:     for (const shadow of parsed._shadow?.recommendations ?? []) {\n682:       recordShadowDelta({\n683:         prompt: `hmac:${key}`,\n684:         recommendation: shadow.skillId,\n685:         liveScore: shadow.liveScore,\n686:         shadowScore: shadow.shadowScore,\n687:         delta: shadow.delta,\n688:         dominantLane: shadow.dominantShadowLane,\n689:         timestamp: parsed.generatedAt,\n690:       });\n691:     }\n692:   }\n693:   advisorPromptCache.set({\n694:     key,\n695:     sourceSignature,\n696:     value: parsed,\n697:     skillLabels: recommendationLabels(parsed),\n698:   });\n699:   return attachTypedCommand(\n700:     input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false\n701:       ? parsed\n702:       : enrichCompiledRoutes(parsed, input.prompt, workspaceRoot, input.options?.surfaceHint, input.options?.compiledRouteTopOnly === true),\n703:     input.prompt,\n704:   );\n705: }\n706: \n707: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n708: // 5. EXPORTS\n709: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n710: \n711: export async function handleAdvisorRecommend(args: unknown): Promise<HandlerResponse> {\n712:   const input = AdvisorRecommendInputSchema.parse(args);\n713:   // Canonicalize via realpath after the schema allowlist check.\n714:   const workspaceRoot = input.workspaceRoot\n715:     ? canonicalizeWorkspaceRoot(input.workspaceRoot)\n716:     : findWorkspaceRoot();\n717:   const effectiveThresholds = publicThresholds({\n718:     confidenceThreshold: input.options?.confidenceThreshold,\n719:     uncertaintyThreshold: input.options?.uncertaintyThreshold,\n720:   });\n721:   const disabledBy = ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS.find((flag) => process.env[flag] === '1');\n722:   const data = disabledBy\n723:     ? disabledOutput(workspaceRoot, effectiveThresholds, disabledBy)\n724:     : await computeRecommendationOutput(input);\n725:   return {\n726:     content: [{\n727:       type: 'text',\n728:       text: JSON.stringify({ status: 'ok', data }, null, 2),\n729:     }],\n730:   };\n731: }\n732: "}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540501767,"end":1794540502452}}}}
